-- allium: 3
-- relay: an operator, a steward (the main role) and the roles they add.
--
-- The record of what happened is an event log, and everything else is the
-- log folded in order.
--
-- Nothing runs between wakes. A dispatcher looks at the roles on every tick
-- and wakes whoever has memos waiting. All work reaches a role as a memo: a
-- routine coming due writes one to its owner. A memo stays open until the
-- role closes it or says they cannot, and a wake that ends with memos still
-- open has failed for those memos, whatever the harness reported.
--
-- There are three ways for work not to get done, and each is handled
-- differently:
--
--   The role cannot do it. They block the memo and it goes to the dead
--   letter handler at once. Trying again would not help.
--
--   The role ran and left it open. The memo is tried again after a wait
--   that doubles, and is dead-lettered when its attempts run out.
--
--   The harness could not run. Its rate limit ran out, it was unreachable,
--   or it needs someone to sign in. That is the harness's failure, so it
--   counts against no memo. The harness is paused, and the wake is carried
--   on from where it stopped.
--
-- Beside the memos relay keeps what it knows: facts that hold over a span of
-- world time and are recorded at a moment of real time, notes and a journal
-- for each role, and docs. It also keeps the operator's board: cards the
-- operator works through over days, which roles and the operator change
-- with ops.
--
-- Every event carries labels, private and contaminated, saying where the
-- text in it came from. A role's session gathers the labels of what it
-- reads. A house role (any role that is not public) may read everything,
-- but no tool it holds can send anything out of the house. A public
-- role, a scout, may reach the web, and its session never holds private
-- at all: it is shown only public text. No call waits for a person.
--
-- This file says what relay does and when. It does not say how the log is
-- stored. The code that decides is the pure function `decide` in core.clj,
-- and where this file and that code disagree the code is right.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Contracts
------------------------------------------------------------

contract HarnessAdapter {
    run: (role: Role, prompt: String) -> HarnessReport

    @invariant RunsAsTheRole
        -- The harness is given the role's standing instructions: the
        -- shared instructions (AGENTS.md), anything the operator added
        -- to them (never for a public role: they carry no labels and may
        -- hold private details), the role's own instructions, and the
        -- role's notes. It knows
        -- which role it is acting as and tells relay so on every tool
        -- call.

    @invariant OffersOnlyTheRolesTools
        -- A role has no file access and no shell of its own. All it can
        -- do is call the tools it has been offered, by name, sh among
        -- them for a house role granted shell (StewardShell). See the
        -- Tools contract.

    @invariant ExitCodeIsNotTheVerdict
        -- A harness can exit cleanly having done nothing. Whether a
        -- memo was handled is decided by whether the role closed it,
        -- never by the exit code.

    @invariant SaysHowItEnded
        -- The report names one outcome: ran, limited, unreachable or
        -- needs_attention. Only ran means the role got to work. The
        -- others are the harness's own failures and are told apart
        -- from a role that ran and did not finish. A limit may say when
        -- it lifts.

    @invariant AHarnessFailureCountsAgainstNoMemo
        -- A wake that ended limited, unreachable or needs_attention
        -- leaves the attempts of its memos as they were, and does not
        -- count towards the runaway guard.

    @invariant StopsAtTheDeadline
        -- A run that outlasts the wake timeout is stopped and reported
        -- as ran and crashed, not as a harness failure. The report
        -- says it was cut short, so the next wake can pick up where
        -- it left off.

    @invariant AFailingAdapterStillEndsTheWake
        -- If the adapter itself throws, the wake is ended as ran and
        -- crashed, and so is one whose program reported something that
        -- is not a report or names an outcome relay does not know. A
        -- harness that is not configured is reported as
        -- needs_attention. A wake that started always ends.
}

contract Channel {
    -- One configured channel (relay.edn :messages :channels): an email
    -- or a push. Each is a pure renderer (relay.channels) and a thin
    -- delivery edge (relay.mail, relay.push). Several messages due on
    -- one channel at once are sent as one.
    deliver: (messages: List<Message>) -> Boolean

    @invariant FailureIsNotFatal
        -- A delivery that fails is recorded as failed and tried again
        -- later. The message is already in the log and in the client,
        -- so nothing is lost.

    @invariant OnlyToItsDestination
        -- A delivery goes only to the channel's configured destination.
        -- An email has exactly one recipient, the configured operator
        -- address, from the configured agent address, no Cc or Bcc,
        -- text/plain only, and no header the model chose except the
        -- subject, encoded on one line (I2).
}

contract Tools {
    -- A role has no file or shell access of its own. Everything it does
    -- is a call to a tool, and every call that changes anything goes
    -- through the same inbound path as that role.

    @invariant ToolsAreNamedAndClassed
        -- Every tool has a name and one class: read (returns content
        -- and sends nothing out), write (changes relay data only),
        -- edit (changes the operator's own things outside relay: nobody
        -- else sees the change and the earlier state survives) or egress
        -- (can send what the model chooses where an outsider can see
        -- it). There is no class for a tool others see, that spends
        -- money or that cannot be undone: no role is given one, and the
        -- settings refuse any other class. relay's own tools that change the registry, routines or dead
        -- letters are write. An external tool also names the
        -- labels its output always carries; the settings refuse a tool
        -- without them, or with a label relay does not know.

    @invariant NoCallWaitsForAPerson
        -- agentloop runs every call at once. The class says where a
        -- tool may go: an egress tool only to a public role, whose
        -- session never holds private (NoWayOutOfTheHouse). The tool's
        -- static labels join the session when the call is decided, and
        -- its result's labels when the result arrives. The settings
        -- refuse the keys always_hold, consent and preview, which relay
        -- no longer has.

    @invariant CallsComeInEnvelopes
        -- A call reaches relay as exactly {input, labels, call_id}, read
        -- by the strict JSON rule of relay acp (ConversationBoundary), the
        -- labels being the calling session's and known to relay, and
        -- its input fitting the tool's parameters. Anything else is
        -- refused before it runs and the model is told only that the
        -- tool failed. The result goes back as {content, is_error,
        -- labels}.

    @invariant ReadsCarryTheLabelsOfWhatTheyShow
        -- A read tool returns the labels of every version whose text it
        -- shows, and of every role id it shows, and private as well
        -- when it shows relay content: a memo, fact, doc, note, journal
        -- entry or routine's instructions. A refusal that quotes stored
        -- text carries that text's labels. Every refusal of a tool call
        -- also carries the calling session's labels, since it may quote
        -- the call itself (an id, a time, a topic, a doc path, the name of
        -- a tool the role lacks) and so show the session its own text.
        -- No refusal is marked as quoting, so a new one cannot miss them.
        -- An error in fixed text from outside relay's refusals (the
        -- clock's, a schema mismatch) carries none. Over-labelling is
        -- allowed; under-labelling never is.

    @invariant AHouseRoleReadsEverything
        -- A read by a role that is not public shows every item as it is,
        -- contaminated ones included, and carries their labels. A role
        -- learns from text from outside freely, improving its own notes
        -- and skills with it, and never does what it asks; the shared
        -- instructions say so.

    @invariant ProvenanceIsWhatAWakeReadDirectly
        -- Every event a role's tool call writes records its sources: the
        -- labels naming an outsider (contaminated, kind:what) of what
        -- that session read directly in its wake and the wakes it
        -- resumed. That is the memos the wakes were for and every result
        -- relay's tool command handed back, each counted by its own
        -- recorded sources (an outside tool's page as web:<page or url>,
        -- a search as search:web; the shell's, none), plus any static
        -- label of an MCP tool the session holds. What its prompt merely
        -- showed (notes, skills, journal tail, fact topics, board) is
        -- not counted. An event that recorded none counts what its
        -- labels name. Labels still carry the full union, for I3. The
        -- operator's reply to a message records no sources, whatever
        -- the message drew on: her verified words are hers. A card
        -- keeps the sources of every event that wrote it, its edits
        -- included.
        -- What the operator is told about where a thing came from, and
        -- which recipe changes the daily note flags, follow sources
        -- only. A message names them once, as a last line ("Drew on:
        -- the web page x; a mail from y"), and only a role's message:
        -- never a subject, the operator's own replies or relay's own
        -- alerts.

    @invariant AScriptHarnessGetsNoTools
        -- A script harness runs a program no policy watches, which could
        -- claim any labels, so a role on one is offered no tools, relay's
        -- own included, and its calls are refused. A role granted tools
        -- may not be put on one.

    @invariant OfferedByGrant
        -- relay's own tools are offered to every role, except these:
        -- adding, updating and removing roles need the may_add grant,
        -- and requeueing dead letters needs the may_add grant or being
        -- the dead letter handler. The operator can define further
        -- external tools in the settings and grant them to roles by
        -- name. A grant to a tool the settings do not define is an
        -- error in the settings.

    @invariant MCPToolsRunInAgentloop
        -- The settings may name MCP servers, and tools taken from them
        -- by the server's name for each, under a name of the operator's.
        -- Such a tool has a class and labels like any other and is
        -- granted by that name; its server gives its description and
        -- schema. agentloop starts the servers a role's granted tools
        -- come from, and no others, and runs the calls itself; relay
        -- refuses a call to one through its own tool command. A server's
        -- secret reaches it as a file agentloop writes from the
        -- server's credentials command, so relay never holds it. relay
        -- refuses settings agentloop would refuse: an unknown server, a
        -- server no tool uses, one server tool under two names, and a
        -- credentials command and {credentials_file} placeholder that do
        -- not come together. Every
        -- call, an MCP one included, is bounded by the harness's tool
        -- timeout, which relay always sends. Each request names, for each
        -- MCP tool, the settings' digest for it, else the one relay
        -- accepted (accepted_tool_digest), else the one the operator's
        -- connection file pinned at connect, so agentloop refuses any
        -- other definition in any session.

    @invariant RemoteServersComeFromConnections
        -- A remote MCP server (one reached over streamable HTTP) is
        -- named by the settings' connections, each a file relay connect
        -- wrote and only the operator edits: the server's URL, which is
        -- https or this machine, the command that prints its access
        -- token, and the tools the operator turned on, each with its
        -- class, labels and the digest of the definition the operator
        -- was shown. No role can read the settings or a connection file.
        -- The access token and the refresh token are kept in the login
        -- keychain and reach agentloop only through the credentials
        -- command's output, never relay's log, request or files.

    @invariant NarrowedArgumentsAreTheOperators
        -- An MCP tool's fixed arguments and hidden arguments are left out
        -- of the schema the model is shown. A call that names one is
        -- refused before the policy decides and before the server sees
        -- anything; every other call reaches the server with the fixed
        -- values as the operator wrote them.

    @invariant AnUnofferedToolIsRefused
        -- A call to a tool the role was not offered is refused,
        -- whatever the harness let through. So is any call by a role
        -- that is no longer active.

    @invariant EnvelopeToolsAnswerInEnvelopes
        -- An external tool with the envelope protocol gets the call on
        -- stdin with the calling session's labels and its call id, and
        -- must print exactly one result envelope, read by the strict
        -- JSON rule (ConversationBoundary), with known labels,
        -- which are added to its static labels. Anything else, a
        -- failure or a timeout tells the model only that it failed.

    @invariant ExternalToolsRunInACleanEnvironment
        -- An external tool gets the call's arguments on its command
        -- line and only PATH, HOME, USER, LANG and TMPDIR from the
        -- environment, so nothing the harness or relay was started
        -- with, such as credentials, reaches it.

    @invariant ExternalToolsRunForALimitedTime
        -- Every external tool, on either protocol, runs for at most its
        -- timeout_seconds, external_tool_timeout when it has none,
        -- counting until it has exited and closed its output. Past that
        -- relay ends the tool and every process it started, a child
        -- that outlived the tool included, with SIGKILL for any that
        -- outlast SIGTERM. A plain
        -- tool's caller is told it timed out; an envelope tool's, only
        -- that it failed.

    @invariant TheClockToolShowsNothingRelayKeeps
        -- clock is a read tool that answers from the time now, the
        -- operator's time zone and its arguments alone: the time, a
        -- date plus a span, the gap between two dates, or the next
        -- given weekday. A date without an offset is in the operator's
        -- zone, for every role: the operator's time zone is not kept
        -- from a public role. Days and months move the calendar, so a day is one
        -- wall-clock day across a daylight saving change; hours and
        -- minutes move the clock. Date-times are read to the second.
        -- The nth weekday counts dates that happen: a date a zone
        -- skipped is not counted.
        -- It reads nothing relay keeps, so its result, and an error from
        -- it, carry no labels. So that an error cannot hand a session's
        -- text back unlabelled, its explanations are fixed text that
        -- never quotes the call, and a number outside the range an
        -- argument allows is refused rather than cast.

    @invariant KnowledgeToolsReadForTheCaller
        -- A role reads and writes its own notes and journal. Facts and
        -- docs are shared by every role.
}

contract Facts {
    -- The questions that can be asked of what relay knows. A fact has two
    -- kinds of time: when it holds in the world (valid_from to valid_to,
    -- either end open) and when each version of it was recorded (the `at`
    -- of the event that wrote it).

    holding_at: (as_of: Timestamp, known_at: Timestamp?, topic: String?, search: String?) -> Set<Fact>
    everything: (known_at: Timestamp?, topic: String?, search: String?) -> Set<Fact>

    @invariant AsOfDefaults
        -- as_of defaults to known_at when only that is given, and to
        -- the time of the latest event when neither is. The tool
        -- defaults it to the current time.

    @invariant HoldingMeansValidAndNotRetracted
        -- A version holds at a time when it is not retracted, its
        -- valid_from is open or not after that time, and its valid_to
        -- is open or after that time. So valid_from is inclusive and
        -- valid_to is exclusive.

    @invariant AsKnownAtUsesTheLatestVersionRecordedByThen
        -- Asked as known at T, each fact is the latest version whose
        -- recording time is not after T, and a fact with no such
        -- version does not exist yet. With no T, the latest version.

    @invariant EverythingIgnoresValidity
        -- everything lists every fact recorded by known_at that is
        -- not retracted, whatever its validity.

    @invariant NoVersionIsEverLost
        -- Supersession, correction and retraction each add a version.
        -- None changes or drops an earlier one, so asking what was
        -- known before still gives the old answer.

    @invariant SupersessionLeavesEarlierAnswersAlone
        -- The old fact ends where the change begins, so every answer
        -- about a time before the change is the same as it was before
        -- the change was recorded. Only times from the change on
        -- differ.

    @invariant AKnownAtQueryIgnoresLaterEvents
        -- Asking what was known at T gives the same answer whatever
        -- was recorded after T, for facts and for docs alike.

    @invariant TopicsAreAHierarchy
        -- A topic matches itself and the topics under it, written
        -- with / between levels. household matches household/car and
        -- not house. Search looks in the text and ranks what it finds
        -- with Okapi BM25 over Porter2 stems, best first, equal scores
        -- by fact id. Only facts sharing a word with the search match;
        -- a search with no words keeps facts whose text contains it,
        -- ignoring case. Every other filter (topic, time, public,
        -- contaminated) applies before the ranking.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

enum CallerKind { operator | dispatcher | role }
enum HarnessCondition { available | limited | unreachable | needs_attention }
enum HarnessOutcome { ran | limited | unreachable | needs_attention }
enum DeadLetterReason { never_closed | blocked | recipient_removed }
enum MessageKind { note | alert | digest | reply }
enum Urgency { low | normal | high }
-- What relay was telling, for its own records; the operator never sees
-- it. A notification an older relay recorded folds into a message with
-- its kind as the origin and nothing left to deliver.
enum MessageOrigin {
    told | memo_for_operator | work_abandoned | runaway_guard_tripped
    | harness_needs_attention | harness_unreachable
    | budget_reached | brief | daily_note | daily_note_acted | github_news
    | tools_unavailable | tool_changed | shown
    | session_forbidden | result_refused | public_role_cannot_run | public_role_can_run
    | turn_unrecorded | conversation_line_dropped | ingest_failing | tool_broken
    | settings_misnamed
}
enum ToolClass { read | write | edit | egress }
enum Label { private | contaminated }
enum FactChange { added | superseded | corrected | retracted }
enum CalendarChange { added | changed | removed }
enum MoveStatus { moving | moved }
enum CardKind { checklist | tracker | note }
enum CardStatus { active | archived }
enum CellState { open | done | skip }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

entity Event {
    -- The record. Every change is an event, and the state of relay is
    -- nothing more than the events folded in order.
    seq: Integer
    -- When it was recorded.
    at: Timestamp
    actor: Caller
    -- Where the text in the event came from: for a role's call, the
    -- calling session's labels; for an event that copies or quotes text
    -- from elsewhere, the labels of that text as well. What the operator
    -- writes or pastes carries none (EntryPointsDecideProvenance).
    labels: Set<Label>
    -- The labels of the session whose call wrote it, for a role.
    session_labels: Set<Label>
    -- The labels of whatever text it copies or quotes.
    copied_labels: Set<Label>
    -- Set by decide on an event that writes an item (a memo, routine,
    -- version of a fact or doc, note or journal entry) whose writer was
    -- public: the operator with --public, or a public role's session.
    -- Never taken from a role's input.
    public: Boolean
}

entity Caller {
    -- Who is asking. The operator and the dispatcher are not roles.
    kind: CallerKind
    role: Role? when kind = role

    is_operator: kind = operator
    is_dispatcher: kind = dispatcher
    -- Granted by the operator's settings and by nobody else.
    may_add: kind = role and role.may_add
    can_requeue: is_operator or may_add or (kind = role and role.id = config.dead_letter_handler)
}

entity Tool {
    name: String
    class: ToolClass
    -- For a tool from an MCP server: the SHA-256 of its definition that
    -- relay accepted, first on trust from the first wake that used it,
    -- then each time agentloop finds it changed (TakeAChangedTool). Null
    -- before its first use.
    accepted_tool_digest: String?
    -- The grant needed to be offered it, if any: relay's own tools that
    -- change the registry or requeue dead letters, and every external tool.
    needs_grant: may_add | dead_letter_handler | named | none
}

entity Harness {
    -- One per named harness in the settings: the program and the limits its
    -- runs are subject to. Every role on a harness shares its state. It has
    -- none until the first run that fails; a run's harness is the one its
    -- role was on when the wake started.
    name: String
    condition: HarnessCondition
    -- The next moment it may be tried. Until then nobody on it is woken
    -- by the dispatcher.
    paused_until: Timestamp?
    -- When it last stopped being available, and how many tries have
    -- failed since.
    down_since: Timestamp?
    failed_tries: Integer
    operator_told: Boolean

    is_paused: paused_until != null and paused_until > now
    is_down: paused_until != null or failed_tries > 0 or down_since != null
}

entity Role {
    -- Chosen when the role is added: lower case letters, digits and
    -- hyphens, starting with a letter, at most 40 characters, and never
    -- operator, dispatcher, relay, all or none. Never reused.
    id: String
    title: String
    -- The role's standing instructions.
    instructions: String
    reports_to: Role?
    -- A harness named in the settings, or the default harness.
    harness_name: String?
    model: String?
    status: active | removed
    -- Granted by the operator's settings and by nobody else, not by
    -- anything a role can write.
    may_add: Boolean
    -- Granted :public in the settings. Its sessions never hold private,
    -- so it is shown only public items. It is the only kind of role that
    -- may have an egress tool, and it may not have may_add, a tool whose
    -- output is private, the dead letter handler's job or a script
    -- harness.
    is_public: Boolean
    -- Granted :shell in the settings: the role is offered sh, which
    -- runs commands in the steward's shell (StewardShell). Never a
    -- public role's, and only with a :house section.
    has_shell: Boolean
    -- Granted :files in the settings: the folders the role may move and
    -- rename files within, with files_move (OrganizeFiles). Separate from
    -- the shell's read-only mounts. Never a public role's.
    files: List<String>
    -- The wake to carry on from, when the last one was cut short.
    interrupted_wake: Wake?
    -- Set when a wake's MCP tools could not be set up, until a wake of
    -- the role runs. The role is tried again at tools_retry_at. A
    -- changed definition sets none of this: relay takes it, unless it
    -- changes again before the role has run (ChangedToolAgain).
    tools_unavailable_session: String?
    tools_retry_at: Timestamp?
    tools_failed_tries: Integer
    -- The tool whose changed definition relay last took for this role,
    -- until a wake of the role runs.
    changed_tool: Tool?
    -- When the operator was last told this role tripped the guard.
    guard_reported_at: Timestamp?

    inbox: Memo with recipient = this
    routines: Routine with owner = this
    wakes: Wake with role = this

    open_memos: inbox where status = unread
    deliverable_memos: inbox where status = unread and not is_hidden
    waiting_memos: inbox where is_waiting
    running_wakes: wakes where status = running
    -- Wakes the role got to work in, within the runaway window. A
    -- conversation counts for nothing, and neither does a wake the harness
    -- failed, which has its own backoff.
    recent_wakes: wakes where started_at + config.runaway_window > now
        and not chat and outcome not in {limited, unreachable, needs_attention}

    -- The one named by harness_name, else the default harness.
    harness: Harness
    -- The tools it is offered, by name.
    offered_tools: Set<Tool>
    -- A role works in one wake at a time, dispatched or asked for by
    -- hand, and keeps one conversation open at a time. A conversation
    -- holds the role only while a turn of it runs.
    working_wakes: running_wakes where not chat
    open_conversations: running_wakes where chat
    -- No other turn of the role's may start: a wake works, or a turn of
    -- its conversation runs. The dispatcher wakes only a role that is
    -- not busy.
    is_busy: working_wakes.count > 0 or (open_conversations where turn = running).count > 0
    -- Any wake of the role runs, an idle conversation included.
    is_open: running_wakes.count > 0
    has_work: waiting_memos.count > 0
    is_waiting_on_tools: tools_unavailable_session != null
        and (tools_retry_at = null or tools_retry_at > now)
    is_paused: harness.is_paused or is_waiting_on_tools
    is_running_away: recent_wakes.count >= config.runaway_wakes

    transitions status {
        active -> removed
        terminal: removed
    }
}

entity Memo {
    -- The event that sent it; its seq is the memo's id.
    sent_by: Event
    sender: Caller
    -- Absent when the memo is to the operator.
    recipient: Role?
    -- The name of the routine whose coming due produced the memo.
    routine: Routine?
    subject: String
    body: String
    sent_at: Timestamp
    status: unread | read | dead
    -- What the role says they did, given when they close it.
    outcome: String when status = read
    closed_at: Timestamp when status = read

    -- How many wakes have carried this memo and ended with it still
    -- open, and the earliest moment the next one may carry it.
    attempts: Integer
    retry_at: Timestamp?
    -- Set when a dead run of a routine was replaced by a newer run, so
    -- that it stays dead.
    superseded_by: Memo?
    -- The labels of the event that sent it.
    labels: Set<Label>
    -- Its sending event was public.
    public: Boolean

    transitions status {
        unread -> read
        unread -> dead
        dead -> unread
        terminal: read
    }

    is_for_operator: recipient = null
    -- A run of a routine that has fired again since.
    is_replaced_run: routine != null and routine.last_run != this
    is_backing_off: retry_at != null and retry_at > now
    -- black box: whether a set of labels holds contaminated.
    is_contaminated: has_contaminated(labels)
    -- A memo to a public role that is not public, or carries private,
    -- is never shown to it. A house role's memo to it is public as
    -- written now (SendAHouseMemoToAPublicRole), so only an older log
    -- holds one, and it waits, unseen, until the operator closes it.
    is_hidden: not is_for_operator and recipient.is_public
        and (not public or has_private(labels))
    is_waiting: status = unread and not is_backing_off and not is_hidden
}

entity Routine {
    -- A routine is identified by its owner and its name. Its name is
    -- lower case letters, digits and hyphens, at most 48 characters.
    owner: Role
    name: String
    -- Stored in a canonical form: "every 30m", "every 2h", "every 1d",
    -- "daily 07:30", "weekly mon 09:00" or "once 2026-10-08 09:00".
    schedule: String
    instructions: String
    -- The moment the schedule is measured from: when the routine was
    -- written, then each time it fires.
    baseline: Timestamp
    -- The memo the routine last fired. It survives the routine being
    -- written again.
    last_run: Memo?
    status: active | retired | removed

    transitions status {
        active -> retired
        active -> removed
        retired -> active
        removed -> active
    }

    -- black box: the first moment strictly after the baseline that the
    -- schedule calls for, in the operator's time zone, or null if there
    -- is none.
    next_due_at: next_occurrence(schedule, baseline)
    is_due: next_due_at != null and next_due_at <= now
    has_open_run: last_run != null and last_run.status = unread
    -- black box: true for a "once" schedule.
    is_one_off: runs_once(schedule)
}

entity Wake {
    -- The id is the seq of the event that started it.
    role: Role
    memos: Set<Memo>
    note: String?
    started_at: Timestamp
    harness_name: String
    -- The process running the wake, to tell whether it is still there.
    pid: Integer?
    pid_start: Timestamp?
    -- True for a conversation with the operator. It carries no memos,
    -- and holds the role only while a turn of it runs.
    chat: Boolean
    -- For a conversation: whether a turn runs now, how many turns have
    -- started, the last that ended, the last the operator has seen, the
    -- ACP session the last turn ran in, and when a turn last started or
    -- ended (when it opened, before its first turn).
    turn: idle | running
    turns: Integer
    turns_ended: Integer
    seen: Integer
    turn_session: String?
    last_activity: Timestamp
    -- How the last turn ended: end_turn, max_tokens, max_turn_requests,
    -- refusal or cancelled (ACP's), error, ended (the conversation
    -- ended during it) or other.
    stop_reason: String?
    status: running | ended
    ended_at: Timestamp when status = ended
    outcome: HarnessOutcome when status = ended
    -- True when the run errored or was stopped at the deadline. Recorded
    -- for whoever reads the history; it decides nothing.
    crashed: Boolean when status = ended
    -- True when the harness stopped the run at the wake deadline. Such a
    -- wake still counts as having run, and is kept to be resumed.
    cut_short: Boolean when status = ended
    said: String?
    -- When a rate limit lifts, if the harness said.
    resets_at: Timestamp?
    -- The harness session a wake ran in, which a later wake can resume.
    session: String?
    -- For a conversation, the harness sessions it used, in the order it
    -- opened them. Empty for a wake.
    sessions: List<String>
    -- The earlier wake this one carries on from, if any.
    resumes: Wake?
    -- The labels its session started with: those of everything in its
    -- prompts.
    seed_labels: Set<Label>
    -- The labels its session ended with, as the harness reported them,
    -- or with none reported, every label it could have gathered.
    labels: Set<Label>
    -- What its model calls used, as the harness reported it. Null for a
    -- conversation, and for a wake from before relay kept it.
    usage: TokenUsage?
    -- Why its MCP tools could not be set up, when they could not:
    -- agentloop's message, cut short and with its links broken, since
    -- it can quote a server, and the server, tool and the pinned and
    -- offered digests where it gave them.
    tools_error: ToolsError?
    -- What its model calls cost in US dollars, as the harness reported
    -- it. Null when the cost is unknown (a model without prices, a
    -- harness that does not say, a wake from before relay kept it);
    -- never taken as 0.
    cost_usd: Decimal?
    -- What the operator said of it with relay flag, oldest first.
    flags: List<WakeFlag>

    transitions status {
        running -> ended
        terminal: ended
    }
}

value WakeFlag {
    value: good | bad
    -- The operator's own words, if any. Never exported in a trace.
    note: String?
    at: Timestamp
}

value ToolsError {
    message: String
    server: String?
    tool: String?
    pinned: String?
    got: String?
}

value TokenUsage {
    input: Integer
    output: Integer
    cache_read: Integer
    cache_write: Integer
}

value WeekSpend {
    -- The Monday the week starts on, at midnight in config.timezone, or
    -- at that Monday's first moment when a clock change skips midnight.
    week: Date
    -- The sum of cost_usd over the wakes that ended in the week, by role.
    cost_usd: Map<Role, Decimal>
    -- The wakes that ran in the week with no cost_usd, by role. Their
    -- cost is unknown, so it is counted beside the sum, never in it.
    unpriced: Map<Role, Integer>
}

entity DeadLetter {
    -- The id is the seq of the event that dead-lettered the memo.
    memo: Memo
    reason: DeadLetterReason
    -- The role's own words when they blocked it.
    explanation: String?
    -- The end of the last transcript, when the memo was never closed.
    transcript_tail: String?
    attempts: Integer
    created_at: Timestamp
    status: open | requeued | superseded

    transitions status {
        open -> requeued
        open -> superseded
        terminal: requeued, superseded
    }
}

value Section {
    heading: String?
    items: List<Item>
}

value Item {
    text: String
    refs: List<Ref>
    labels: Set<Label>
}

entity Message {
    -- What relay tells the operator, one data model whatever carries
    -- it. The id is the seq of the event that recorded it.
    kind: MessageKind
    urgency: Urgency
    -- One line.
    subject: String
    -- Each section an optional heading and items; each item its text,
    -- the refs it drew on, and where it came from (its labels, shown to
    -- the operator in plain words). At most 12 sections of at most 50
    -- items of at most 4000 characters: tell_operator is refused past
    -- them, and relay's own messages are cut to fit, saying how many
    -- items or sections were left out.
    sections: List<Section>
    in_reply_to: Message?
    -- The first message of its thread.
    thread: Message
    -- The operator's own replies to it, verified by the channel they
    -- came through (OperatorMail), oldest first.
    replies: List<String>
    origin: MessageOrigin
    -- The role that told her (tell_operator); none for relay's own.
    told_by: Role?
    about: Role?
    harness: Harness?
    memo: Memo?
    dead_letter: DeadLetter?
    -- For budget_reached: the week, by its Monday, and the share of
    -- the weekly budget it reached, 80 or 100.
    week: Date?
    percent: Integer?
    -- For brief and daily_note: the day it covers.
    date: Date?
    -- For daily_note: what each number in it stands for, a change to
    -- undo or a suggestion to drop, and which were done.
    numbered: List<NoteItem>
    created_at: Timestamp
    -- One per configured channel its route names, with when it is due
    -- (route). The client channel is not among them: every message is
    -- always the client's to show (_relay/messages).
    deliveries: List<Delivery>
    -- The operator's answers (ReplyToAMessage), oldest first.
    replies: List<Reply>
    -- For an alert: set when the trouble it told of is over
    -- (ResolveAlerts). A resolved alert is no longer ready for her.
    resolved: Timestamp?
}

value Reply {
    -- The operator's answer to a message, from a channel, as she gave it.
    channel: String
    text: String
    created_at: Timestamp
}

entity Delivery {
    message: Message
    channel: String
    due: Timestamp
    status: pending | delivered | failed
    -- Failed tries so far, and when the next is due; none once relay
    -- has given up.
    attempts: Integer
    retry_at: Timestamp?

    transitions status {
        pending -> delivered
        pending -> failed
        failed -> delivered
        terminal: delivered
    }
}

entity DailyNote {
    -- That relay made a day's note, whether or not it had anything to
    -- say. At most one a day. A morning brief an older relay recorded
    -- (brief/composed) folds into one.
    date: Date
    sent: Boolean
    -- The changes it flagged, by the seq of the event that made each.
    flagged: List<RecipeChange>
    created_at: Timestamp
}

entity NoteItem {
    n: Integer
    op: revert | dismiss
    change: RecipeChange?        -- for revert
    keys: List<String>           -- for dismiss: the suggestion's keys
    done: reverted | dismissed | null
}

entity RecipeChange {
    -- A change to how a role works, kept as relay folds the event that
    -- made it: a skill (a doc under skills/<role>/), a routine, a note
    -- a role keeps, or a role. The id is that event's seq.
    what: skill | routine | note | role
    change: added | changed | removed
    owner: Role
    name: String
    actor: String
    labels: Set<String>
    -- What it replaced: the earlier version, or null when it made
    -- something new.
    before: String?
    -- The change before it to the same thing, or null for the first.
    prior: RecipeChange?
    reverted: Boolean
    -- The change this one undid, when an undo made it.
    undo_of: RecipeChange?
}

entity NotePart {
    -- What the note's role wrote for the next note, one per part, the
    -- latest write replacing the one before.
    part: ahead | grants | github | learned
    items: List<String>
    labels: Set<String>
}

entity Dismissed {
    -- A suggestion the operator turned down, by key.
    key: String
    text: String
}

entity Fact {
    -- The id is the seq of the event that created it.
    -- The fact this one replaced, when the world changed. Retracting this
    -- fact leaves the link and restores the old one.
    supersedes: Fact?
    versions: FactVersion with fact = this

    -- The latest version; what the record says now.
    current: versions.latest
    is_retracted: current.change = retracted
    is_superseded: current.superseded_by != null
}

entity FactVersion {
    fact: Fact
    -- The seq of the event that wrote this version.
    seq: Integer
    recorded_at: Timestamp
    actor: Caller
    change: FactChange
    topic: String?
    text: String
    -- When it holds in the world. Either end may be open.
    valid_from: Timestamp?
    valid_to: Timestamp?
    -- Required for a correction or retraction.
    why: String? when change in {corrected, retracted}
    superseded_by: Fact?
}

entity CalendarEvent {
    -- An event on the agent's own calendar. The id is the seq of the event
    -- that added it, and makes its UID in the feed, so the UID never
    -- changes. Versioned like a fact; no version is dropped.
    versions: CalendarEventVersion with event = this

    current: versions.latest
    is_removed: current.change = removed
    -- The feed's SEQUENCE: how many changes it has had.
    sequence: versions.count - 1
}

entity CalendarEventVersion {
    event: CalendarEvent
    seq: Integer
    recorded_at: Timestamp
    actor: Role
    change: CalendarChange
    title: String
    start: Timestamp
    end: Timestamp
    -- An all-day event's first day and the day after its last; start and
    -- end are then the starts of those days in the operator's zone.
    start_date: Date?
    end_date: Date?
    location: String?
    description: String?
    why: String?
}

entity MoveCall {
    -- One files_move call. The id is the seq of its files/moving event,
    -- recorded before anything moves; files/moved records what it did.
    -- A call relay never finished stays moving, and undo then tells the
    -- operator to check its moves by hand.
    actor: Role
    moves: List<MovePlan>
    -- The real paths of the folders the actor was granted when the call
    -- was made. The ready view and relay moves show paths relative to
    -- them, under the folder's short name. A call recorded before this
    -- has none, and is shown relative to the folder its files share.
    roots: List<String>?
    status: MoveStatus
    done: List<MoveStep>
    undone: Set<Integer>
    stopped: String?
}

value MovePlan {
    -- Real paths, links resolved, both inside one of the actor's folders.
    from: String
    to: String
}

value MoveStep {
    index: Integer
    -- Sizes and SHA-256 of what moved, a folder's every entry included.
    fingerprint: Fingerprint
    -- The folders the move made for its target, which undo removes once
    -- they are empty again.
    created: List<String>
}

entity Prepared {
    -- What a role prepared for the operator with an edit tool that is not
    -- relay's own, such as a draft in her account. Recorded from the role's
    -- session after the wake or the conversation turn (RecordWhatWasPrepared),
    -- once per call. The id is the seq of the event that recorded it.
    role: Role
    tool: String
    call: String
    -- The input's subject, title, name or summary, else the tool's name in words.
    title: String
    -- The first line of the tool's result: where it put the thing.
    place: String
    -- A start of the input's body, text, content or description.
    preview: String?
    recorded_at: Timestamp
}

entity Note {
    -- A role's note: named, and shown in the role's prompt at every wake.
    owner: Role
    name: String
    text: String
    written_at: Timestamp
}

entity JournalEntry {
    -- Append only. The id is the seq of the event that wrote it.
    owner: Role
    text: String
    at: Timestamp
}

entity Doc {
    -- Longer shared content, by path.
    path: String
    versions: DocVersion with doc = this

    -- The latest version; a removal is a version too.
    current: versions.latest
    is_present: not current.removed
}

-- The operator's board. There is one board, and every active card is
-- on it. Cards are private only: a public role is not offered the card
-- tools, and a card command from a public role's session is refused. A
-- card change never wakes a role and never notifies anyone.
entity Card {
    -- The id is the seq of the event that added it.
    kind: CardKind
    title: CardText
    -- The role that added it, or the operator.
    owner: Caller
    added_at: Timestamp
    -- The seq of the last event that changed it.
    rev: Integer
    status: CardStatus

    items: List<CardItem> when kind = checklist
    rows: List<CardElement> when kind = tracker
    columns: List<CardElement> when kind = tracker
    -- Cells that are not open, by row and column. A cell not listed is open.
    cells: Set<Cell> when kind = tracker
    note: CardText when kind = note

    -- The next id for each kind of element. Ids are never reused, and
    -- decide assigns them and writes them into the event.
    next_item: Integer when kind = checklist
    next_row: Integer when kind = tracker
    next_column: Integer when kind = tracker

    is_complete:
        (kind = checklist and items.count > 0 and items.all(i => i.done))
        or (kind = tracker and rows.count * columns.count > 0
            and cells.count = rows.count * columns.count)

    -- What reading the card adds: private, and the labels of the text it
    -- shows now. Ticks, cell states, archive and restore carry no text,
    -- so they add none.
    labels: {private} + title.labels + items.labels + rows.labels + columns.labels + note.labels
}

value CardText {
    -- One line of 1 to card_line_length characters, except a note's
    -- text, which may be empty and run to card_note_length. Characters
    -- are Unicode code points, so an emoji counts as one.
    text: String
    -- The labels and seq of the event that last wrote this text.
    labels: Set<Label>
    rev: Integer
}

value CardElement {
    -- An item, row or column: a number of the card's own, and its text.
    id: Integer
    text: CardText
}

value CardItem {
    id: Integer
    text: CardText
    done: Boolean
}

value Cell {
    row: Integer
    column: Integer
    state: CellState   -- done or skip; open is not stored
}

-- Skills. A role's skills are the docs under skills/<role id>/, each with
-- a `# Title` first line and a line starting `Use when:`. A role writes
-- or removes docs there only for its own id, and elsewhere under skills/
-- not at all; the operator may write any. black box: true for a caller
-- who is not a role, for any path outside skills/, and for a role whose
-- id is the second segment of a path under skills/.
-- The system prompt lists each of a role's skills by title and use-when
-- line, and the wake carries their labels. A public role is listed its
-- public skills only.

-- Refs. A ref is [[kind:id]]: a kind from the list below and an id the
-- kind defines (fact number, doc path with an optional @version, a note
-- as role/name, memo, journal and card numbers, shown/<date>/<call>,
-- and for rem, file and web the reminder id, path or URL). Resolving one
-- against the state gives :ok with the item's title, text and labels,
-- :missing, or :external for the kinds relay cannot look up.
value Ref {
    kind: fact | doc | note | memo | journal | rem | file | web | shown | card
    id: String
}

entity DocVersion {
    doc: Doc
    -- The seq of the event that wrote this version.
    seq: Integer
    at: Timestamp
    actor: Caller
    content: String when not removed
    removed: Boolean
    -- Set on a version that keeps a display: its call, title and sources.
    shown: ShownDisplay?
}

value ShownDisplay {
    call: String
    title: String
    sources: List<Source>
}

value Source {
    title: String
    ref: String
}


------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    wake_timeout: Duration = 30.minutes

    -- Retrying a memo. The wait doubles after each failed attempt,
    -- starting at retry_base and never exceeding retry_ceiling.
    max_attempts: Integer = 8
    retry_base: Duration = 1.minute
    retry_ceiling: Duration = 1.hour

    -- How long a harness stays paused when a run hit the limit without
    -- saying when it resets. The next wake after that finds out.
    limit_probe_interval: Duration = 15.minutes

    -- How long an unreachable harness is waited out before the operator
    -- is told.
    outage_patience: Duration = 2.hours

    -- The role that is told about dead letters and decides what to do
    -- with them. When it is absent, or is not an active role, dead
    -- letters go to the operator.
    dead_letter_handler: String = "steward"

    -- The harness a role runs on when it names none.
    default_harness: String = "agentloop"

    -- A last resort against a role stuck in a loop. It is set far above
    -- ordinary use and is not meant to ration it.
    runaway_wakes: Integer = 30
    runaway_window: Duration = 1.hour

    -- How long a delivery due when its message was made may sit
    -- undelivered before the tick makes it. Fixed in the dispatcher, not a setting.
    stranded_after: Duration = 2.minutes

    -- Limits on what is written.
    max_subject_length: Integer = 200
    max_fact_length: Integer = 2000
    -- Events the feed carries at once: live ones not over for more than 30
    -- days, and removed ones still listed as cancelled.
    max_calendar_events: Integer = 1000
    max_note_length: Integer = 4000
    max_journal_entry_length: Integer = 20000
    max_doc_length: Integer = 500000

    -- How many times a delivery is tried before relay gives up.
    delivery_attempts: Integer = 8

    -- What the roles may spend in a week, all together, in US dollars,
    -- from :budget {:weekly-usd n} in the settings. Null for none. relay
    -- only warns as spend nears it (WarnOfSpend).
    weekly_budget: Decimal? = null

    -- When the daily note is made each day, in the time zone, and the
    -- role that writes its suggestions, from :daily-note {:at "07:30"
    -- :role "steward"} in the settings. Null for no note. The role may
    -- not be public. :brief is refused, with a pointer to :daily-note.
    daily_note_at: Time? = null
    daily_note_role: Role? = null
    -- The routine that searches for grants, from :grants "owner/name" in
    -- :daily-note. When nobody wrote the note's Grants part, relay says
    -- from that routine's wakes since the last note whether the search
    -- has not run, ran with the web search key failing (a tool/broken
    -- event for the wake, or the key still not set up), or ran and
    -- found nothing.
    daily_note_grants: String? = null
    -- How long an external tool may run when it has no timeout_seconds.
    external_tool_timeout: Duration = 10.minutes

    -- The board.
    max_active_cards: Integer = 30
    card_line_length: Integer = 200
    card_note_length: Integer = 8000
    max_checklist_items: Integer = 100
    max_tracker_rows: Integer = 40
    max_tracker_columns: Integer = 24
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The registry

rule AddRole {
    when: RoleAddRequested(caller, id, title?, instructions, reports_to?, harness?, model?)

    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.may_add
    requires: is_usable_id(id)   -- black box: the id pattern above
    -- ids are never reused: a removed role keeps its id.
    requires: not exists Role{id: id}
    requires: instructions != ""
    requires: harness = null or is_configured_harness(harness)   -- black box: named in the settings

    -- A role added by a role reports to it, unless told otherwise. One
    -- added by the operator reports to nobody unless told.
    let manager = reports_to ?? default_manager(caller)   -- black box: the caller if it is a role, else nobody
    requires: manager = null or manager.status = active

    ensures: Role.created(
        id: id,
        title: title ?? id,
        instructions: instructions,
        reports_to: manager,
        harness_name: harness,
        model: model,
        status: active,
        may_add: false
    )
}

rule UpdateRole {
    when: RoleUpdateRequested(caller, role, title?, instructions?, reports_to?, harness?, model?)

    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.may_add
    requires: role.status = active
    requires: caller.role != role
    requires: title != null or instructions != null or reports_to != null
        or harness != null or model != null
    requires: instructions = null or instructions != ""
    requires: harness = null or is_configured_harness(harness)
    requires: reports_to = null or reports_to?.status = active

    ensures:
        role.title = title ?? role.title
        role.instructions = instructions ?? role.instructions
        role.reports_to = reports_to ?? role.reports_to
        role.harness_name = harness ?? role.harness_name
        role.model = model ?? role.model

    @guidance
        -- A role cannot change itself, so it cannot widen its own
        -- standing instructions.
}

rule RemoveRole {
    when: RoleRemoveRequested(caller, role)

    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.may_add
    requires: role.status = active
    requires: caller.role != role
    requires: not role.is_open

    ensures: role.status = removed

    -- Its routines stop.
    ensures:
        for routine in role.routines where status = active:
            routine.status = removed

    -- Its open memos are dead-lettered, so the work is not lost.
    ensures:
        for memo in role.open_memos:
            MemoDeadLettered(memo: memo, reason: recipient_removed)

    @guidance
        -- A role that is running now cannot be removed, and neither can
        -- one with a conversation open between turns; remove it once it
        -- stops. A removed role can no longer act, and its id is
        -- never given out again. If the removed role was the dead letter
        -- handler, its own dead letters go to the operator.
}

-- Memos

rule SendMemo {
    when: MemoSendRequested(caller, recipient, subject, body)

    requires: recipient.status = active
    requires: subject != ""
    requires: not has_newline(subject)   -- black box
    requires: subject.length <= config.max_subject_length
    requires: body != ""

    ensures: Memo.created(
        sender: caller,
        recipient: recipient,
        subject: subject,
        body: body,
        sent_at: now,
        status: unread,
        attempts: 0
    )

    @guidance
        -- Anyone may send, the dispatcher included. Subject and body
        -- are trimmed and must not be blank.
}

rule SendAHouseMemoToAPublicRole {
    when: MemoSendRequested(caller, recipient, subject, body)

    requires: not caller.is_operator
    requires: caller.kind = role
    requires: not caller.is_public
    requires: recipient.is_public
    requires: not has_private(caller.id_labels)

    ensures: Memo.created(
        sender: caller,
        recipient: recipient,
        subject: subject,
        body: body,
        sent_at: now,
        status: unread,
        attempts: 0,
        public: true,
        labels: without_private(session_labels(caller))
    )

    @guidance
        -- Decision 6: a house role's request to a scout goes as written,
        -- with no sign-off. The role chose what to put in it, and is
        -- told that it went out as written. It keeps its other labels
        -- and its sources, so a request shaped by a mail still says
        -- where it came from. A role
        -- whose id was written in private cannot send one, since the
        -- scout would be shown its name: "<to> works on the open web
        -- and is never shown a name written in private, as <role>'s
        -- was, so the memo was not sent." A private memo to a public
        -- role from an older log stays unseen by it.
}

rule SendAPublicRoleMemo {
    when: MemoSendRequested(caller, recipient, subject, body)

    requires: caller.is_public
    requires: recipient = operator or role_text_public(recipient)
        or exists memo in Memos where memo.recipient = caller and memo.sender = recipient
            and shown_to_public(memo)

    ensures: Memo.created(
        sender: caller,
        recipient: recipient,
        subject: subject,
        body: body,
        sent_at: now,
        status: unread,
        attempts: 0,
        labels: session_labels(caller) + {contaminated}
    )

    @guidance
        -- What a scout sends is from the web, even from a session that
        -- has read nothing yet. It may answer a role that wrote to it.
}

rule SendMemoToOperator {
    when: MemoToOperatorSendRequested(caller, subject, body)

    requires: subject != ""
    requires: not has_newline(subject)
    requires: subject.length <= config.max_subject_length
    requires: body != ""

    ensures: Memo.created(
        sender: caller,
        recipient: null,
        subject: subject,
        body: body,
        sent_at: now,
        status: unread,
        attempts: 0
    )

    @guidance
        -- The operator is addressed by the name "operator", which no
        -- role can have.
}

rule NotifyOperatorOfMemo {
    when: memo: Memo.created

    requires: memo.is_for_operator

    ensures: Message.created(
        origin: memo_for_operator,
        kind: note,
        urgency: normal,
        subject: memo.subject,
        sections: [memo.body],
        memo: memo,
        created_at: now,
        deliveries: route(this, now)
    )

    @guidance
        -- A memo to the operator always becomes a message, once: a
        -- note with the memo's subject and its body as the one item.
}

rule ReplyToAMessage {
    -- The one path for the operator's answer to a message, whatever
    -- channel brought it: the client channel (_relay/reply, relay reply)
    -- or her verified mail (OperatorMail). Each channel checks in code
    -- that the reply is hers and cleans the text (sanitize) first.
    when: MessageReplied(message, channel, text)

    requires: message.told_by != null or message.origin = daily_note
        -- a role told her; relay's own messages have nobody to answer,
        -- except the daily note, whose writer (config.daily_note_role) hears it
    requires: text.length > 0

    ensures: message.replies = message.replies + Reply(channel: channel, text: text, created_at: now)
    ensures: Memo.created(
        from: operator,
        to: message.told_by,   -- for mail, the source's role when that one is gone or public
        subject: "Re: " + message.subject,
        body: text,   -- and a line naming the message, and tell_operator's in_reply_to
        sent_at: now,
        status: unread,
        attempts: 0
    )
    if message.memo != null and message.memo.to = operator and message.memo.status = unread:
        ensures: message.memo.status = read   -- answered; closed by the operator
    if message.origin = daily_note:
        ensures: what the reply asks for ("revert N", "not N") is done
            (RevertChange, DismissSuggestion), and relay answers once in the
            thread with what it did, on the reply's own channel only (the
            client alone for a reply from the client)
        if the reply says nothing but "revert N" and "not N":
            ensures: no memo is sent; relay has done all it asks

    @guidance
        -- The reply is the operator's own, so the memo is trusted (I5). It
        -- carries the labels of the message whose subject it quotes. From
        -- the client channel the role must still be active and not
        -- public, and the reply is at most 4000 characters.
}

rule RecordWhatWasPrepared {
    when: EditCallRead(caller, tool, call, input, result, session_labels)

    requires: caller.kind = role
    requires: not caller.is_public
    requires: tool.class = edit and not tool.is_relays_own
    requires: not exists Prepared{tool: tool, call: call}

    ensures: Prepared.created(
        role: caller,
        tool: tool,
        call: call,
        title: title_of(input, tool),   -- black box: subject, title, name or summary, else the tool's name in words
        place: first_line(result),
        preview: preview_of(input),   -- black box: body, text, content or description
        recorded_at: now
    )

    @guidance
        -- The dispatcher reads the session after a wake and as a
        -- conversation goes, and records each call that was allowed and
        -- ended without an error. The record carries the labels the
        -- session held at the call, so the ready view says where the
        -- thing came from. Nothing waits for it.
}

rule PublicItem {
    when: event: Event.created

    requires: writes_an_item(event)   -- black box: a memo, routine, fact or doc version, note or journal entry

    ensures: event.public = ((event.actor.is_operator and asked_for_public(event))   -- black box: --public
                             or (event.actor.kind = role
                                 and calling_wake_began_public(event)))   -- black box: see guidance
                            and copies_only_public_text(event)   -- black box: what it copies is public

    @guidance
        -- A role's id, title and instructions are public when the
        -- operator wrote them with --public; rewriting both title and
        -- instructions so vouches for the id. A public role sees only
        -- roles whose text is public, and its own must be, or it is not
        -- woken and the operator is told once how to fix it.
        -- A role's call is a public writer's only when it comes from the
        -- wake relay named in the harness's tool command, that wake is
        -- running, and it began while the role was public, whether or not
        -- relay.edn still says so: such a session only ever saw public
        -- text. It is read for as public, and refused private, as long
        -- as relay.edn or that wake says it is public. A session
        -- from before the role was public may hold private text no label
        -- records (the operator's AGENTS.md, what was said in it).
        -- A public item's read labels are its own, with no private
        -- floor. An item that copies text (a supersession or correction
        -- of a fact, a revert, a routine's run) is public only when what
        -- it copies is; a writer who asked for public is refused rather
        -- than given a private item, and a revert is as public as the
        -- version it restores. The dispatcher writes nothing public of
        -- its own: a dead letter never is, and a routine's run is when
        -- the routine is.
}

rule RefuseWhatAPublicRoleMayNotHold {
    when: CommandRequested(caller, command)   -- black box: any command

    requires: refused_for_a_public_role(caller, command)

    ensures: Rejected(command)

    @guidance
        -- Everything that would put private into a public role's session
        -- is refused where it would happen, never dropped or quietly made
        -- private: a public role's call from a session holding private;
        -- a memo, routine, note, journal entry or wake note for it from
        -- the operator without --public; a role id, title or
        -- instructions for it from anyone but the operator, since any
        -- other role's session may carry the operator's unlabelled
        -- AGENTS.md; a wake of it whose own text the operator did not
        -- write, or whose prompts would hold private; a doc it would
        -- write over that it cannot see; and a memo to it from a house
        -- role whose own id was written in private
        -- (SendAHouseMemoToAPublicRole).
        -- Its reads show only public items, the roles whose text the
        -- operator wrote, and docs whose path was chosen in public, and
        -- leave out everything else without a trace: a fact, doc or memo it cannot see does
        -- not exist for it, and a search does not look in one. relay's
        -- tool command replaces any result for it that carries private
        -- with a refusal, and the request tells agentloop to forbid
        -- private as well, so agentloop refuses such a result, refuses a
        -- session that holds private, and reports both. The operator's time zone is not private: a public role is told
        -- times in it, in its prompts and by the clock tool, and its
        -- routines follow it, as for any role.
        -- No session from before a role was public is carried on once it
        -- is, since such a session may hold private text no label
        -- records: an interrupted wake starts afresh, and its
        -- conversations are kept apart.
}

rule RevertFact {
    when: FactRevertRequested(caller, fact, version)

    requires: caller.is_operator
    requires: version.fact = fact

    ensures: FactVersion.created(
        fact: fact,
        recorded_at: now,
        actor: caller,
        change: corrected,
        topic: version.topic,
        text: version.text,
        valid_from: version.valid_from,
        valid_to: version.valid_to,
        superseded_by: version.superseded_by
    )

    @guidance
        -- The restored version carries the labels of the version it
        -- copies.
}

rule RevertDoc {
    when: DocRevertRequested(caller, doc, version)

    requires: caller.is_operator
    requires: version.doc = doc

    ensures: DocVersion.created(
        doc: doc,
        at: now,
        actor: caller,
        content: version.content,
        removed: version.removed
    )
}

-- What the operator was shown

rule KeepADisplay {
    when: DisplayShown(caller, ref, title, body, sources, call)

    requires: caller.kind = role
    requires: is_shown_ref(ref)   -- black box: shown:<yyyy-mm-dd>/<id>, the id lower case letters, digits, _ and -, at most 100
    let path = shown_path(ref)    -- black box: shown/<yyyy-mm-dd>/<id>.md
    requires: not exists Doc{path: path}

    ensures:
        let doc = Doc.created(path: path)
        DocVersion.created(
            doc: doc,
            at: now,
            actor: caller,
            content: shown_doc_text(title, body, sources),   -- black box: the title as a heading, the body, the sources as refs
            removed: false,
            shown: ShownDisplay(call: call, title: title, sources: sources)
        )

    @guidance
        -- A tool result may carry a display, which agentloop keeps apart
        -- from the model: the model is told only its ref. After a wake,
        -- and as a conversation goes, the dispatcher reads each display
        -- from the session's entries and keeps it here, as the role whose
        -- session made it, with the display's labels (its own, the
        -- result's and the session's as the call ran). The same display
        -- again records nothing; another at its path is refused. Nobody
        -- puts a doc under shown/ any other way, so a doc there is always
        -- what the operator was shown. A wake that kept displays tells
        -- the operator their paths, never their text; a conversation's
        -- operator saw them as they came.
}

rule CloseMemo {
    when: MemoCloseRequested(caller, memo, outcome)

    requires: memo.status = unread
    -- The recipient closes it, and so can the operator, whoever it is for.
    requires: caller.is_operator or (caller.role != null and caller.role = memo.recipient)
    requires: outcome != ""

    ensures:
        memo.status = read
        memo.outcome = outcome
        memo.closed_at = now
        memo.retry_at = null

    @guidance
        -- The operator closes their own memos once dealt with, so their
        -- inbox only ever holds what is waiting. Closing is how a role
        -- says "I did this". It can happen during a wake or in a
        -- conversation, and it stands even if the wake it happened in
        -- later crashes.
}

rule BlockMemo {
    when: MemoBlockRequested(caller, memo, explanation)

    requires: caller.role != null and caller.role.status = active
    requires: memo.status = unread
    requires: memo.recipient = caller.role
    requires: explanation != ""

    ensures: MemoDeadLettered(memo: memo, reason: blocked, explanation: explanation)

    @guidance
        -- Blocking is how a role says "I cannot do this". It skips the
        -- retries, since trying again would not help. The operator
        -- cannot block, having nobody to pass it to.
}

rule DeadLetterMemo {
    when: MemoDeadLettered(memo, reason, explanation?, transcript_tail?, wake?)

    ensures: memo.status = dead
    ensures: memo.retry_at = null
    ensures: DeadLetter.created(
        memo: memo,
        reason: reason,
        explanation: explanation,
        transcript_tail: transcript_tail,
        attempts: memo.attempts,
        created_at: now,
        status: open
    )
}

rule EscalateToHandler {
    when: letter: DeadLetter.created

    let handler = Role{id: config.dead_letter_handler}

    requires: exists handler and handler.status = active
    requires: letter.memo.recipient != handler

    ensures: Memo.created(
        sender: dispatcher,
        recipient: handler,
        subject: "Dead letter: " + dead_letter_title(letter),   -- black box: see guidance
        body: dead_letter_report(letter),                       -- black box: see guidance
        sent_at: now,
        status: unread,
        attempts: 0
    )

    @guidance
        -- The report says whose memo it was and who sent it, gives the
        -- reason (the role's explanation if they blocked it, the number
        -- of wakes if they never closed it, or that the recipient was
        -- removed), tells the handler to work out why and either fix
        -- the cause and requeue the memo or take it to the operator,
        -- and quotes the memo and the end of the last transcript.
}

rule TellOperatorOfTheirRequest {
    when: letter: DeadLetter.created

    requires: letter.memo.sender = operator

    ensures: Message.created(
        origin: work_abandoned,
        kind: alert,
        urgency: normal,
        subject: "Could not finish " + letter.memo.subject,
        sections: [why_and_how_to_retry(letter)],          -- black box: see guidance
        about: letter.memo.recipient,
        dead_letter: letter,
        created_at: now,
        deliveries: route(this, now)
    )

    @guidance
        -- The operator asked for it, so they hear at once, once: the
        -- reason in a line and the relay retry that tries again. The
        -- handler still gets the dead letter (EscalateToHandler), and
        -- its report says the operator was told.
}

rule EscalateToOperator {
    when: letter: DeadLetter.created

    let handler = Role{id: config.dead_letter_handler}

    requires: not exists handler or handler.status != active or letter.memo.recipient = handler
    -- Told already by TellOperatorOfTheirRequest, directly or for the
    -- request a dead letter's memo is about.
    requires: request_of(letter.memo).sender != operator

    ensures: Message.created(
        origin: work_abandoned,
        kind: alert,
        urgency: normal,
        subject: dead_letter_title(letter),
        sections: [dead_letter_report(letter)],
        about: letter.memo.recipient,
        dead_letter: letter,
        created_at: now,
        deliveries: route(this, now)
    )

    @guidance
        -- When the handler's own work is dead-lettered, or there is no
        -- handler, there is nobody left to escalate to but the
        -- operator. A dead letter's memo names the letter it is about,
        -- so a dead letter of a dead letter is told by the subject of
        -- the request at the bottom of the chain (request_of), never as
        -- "Dead letter: ... could not finish ...".
}

rule RequeueMemos {
    when: RetryRequested(caller, role)

    requires: caller.can_requeue
    requires: role.status = active

    for memo in role.inbox:
        requires: memo.status = dead
        requires: memo.superseded_by = null
        requires: not memo.is_replaced_run
        ensures:
            memo.status = unread
            memo.attempts = 0
            memo.retry_at = null

    @guidance
        -- The operator, the dead letter handler and roles granted
        -- may_add can do this. The memo comes back with a clean slate.
}

rule SupersedeReplacedRuns {
    when: RetryRequested(caller, role)

    requires: caller.can_requeue
    requires: role.status = active

    -- A dead routine run that a newer run of the same routine has
    -- replaced is not brought back, or the routine would have two open
    -- runs. It stays dead, marked as superseded.
    for memo in role.inbox:
        requires: memo.status = dead
        requires: memo.superseded_by = null
        requires: memo.is_replaced_run
        ensures: memo.superseded_by = memo.routine.last_run
}

rule CloseRequeuedLetters {
    when: RetryRequested(caller, role)

    requires: caller.can_requeue
    requires: role.status = active

    for letter in DeadLetters where memo.recipient = role:
        requires: letter.status = open
        requires: letter.memo.status = dead
        requires: not letter.memo.is_replaced_run
        ensures: letter.status = requeued
}

rule CloseSupersededLetters {
    when: RetryRequested(caller, role)

    requires: caller.can_requeue
    requires: role.status = active

    for letter in DeadLetters where memo.recipient = role:
        requires: letter.status = open
        requires: letter.memo.status = dead
        requires: letter.memo.is_replaced_run
        ensures: letter.status = superseded
}

-- Routines

rule WriteRoutine {
    when: RoutineWriteRequested(caller, owner, name, schedule, instructions)

    -- A role writes its own routines. The operator names the role.
    requires: owner.status = active
    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.role = owner
    requires: is_usable_routine_name(name)   -- black box: the name pattern above
    requires: parses_as_schedule(schedule)    -- black box: the five forms above
    requires: instructions != ""

    requires: not exists Routine{owner: owner, name: name}

    ensures: Routine.created(
        owner: owner,
        name: name,
        schedule: canonical_schedule(schedule),
        instructions: instructions,
        baseline: now,
        status: active
    )

    @guidance
        -- Anything that is not a schedule is refused when it is
        -- written, not left to never come due.
}

rule RewriteRoutine {
    when: RoutineWriteRequested(caller, owner, name, schedule, instructions)

    let routine = Routine{owner: owner, name: name}

    requires: exists routine
    requires: routine.status = active
    requires: owner.status = active
    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.role = owner
    requires: parses_as_schedule(schedule)
    requires: instructions != ""

    ensures:
        routine.schedule = canonical_schedule(schedule)
        routine.instructions = instructions
        routine.baseline = now

    @guidance
        -- Writing a routine again replaces it and restarts its clock,
        -- also if it had retired or been removed. Its last run is kept,
        -- so a run that is still open still holds back the next one.
}

rule ReviveRoutine {
    when: RoutineWriteRequested(caller, owner, name, schedule, instructions)

    let routine = Routine{owner: owner, name: name}

    requires: exists routine
    requires: routine.status = retired or routine.status = removed
    requires: owner.status = active
    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.role = owner
    requires: parses_as_schedule(schedule)
    requires: instructions != ""

    ensures:
        routine.schedule = canonical_schedule(schedule)
        routine.instructions = instructions
        routine.baseline = now
        routine.status = active

    @guidance
        -- A routine that retired or was removed comes back when it is
        -- written again, with its clock restarted. Its last run is
        -- kept, so a run still open still holds back the next one.
}

rule RemoveRoutine {
    when: RoutineRemoveRequested(caller, routine)

    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.role = routine.owner
    requires: routine.status = active

    ensures: routine.status = removed
}

rule FireRoutines {
    when: DispatcherTicks(lost_wakes)

    for routine in Routines where owner.status = active and status = active and is_due and not has_open_run:
        ensures:
            let run = Memo.created(
                sender: dispatcher,
                recipient: routine.owner,
                routine: routine,
                subject: routine.name,
                body: routine.instructions,
                sent_at: now,
                status: unread,
                attempts: 0
            )
            routine.baseline = now
            routine.last_run = run

    @guidance
        -- A routine is a memo its owner sends themselves on a
        -- schedule, so it is retried, blocked and dead-lettered like any
        -- other memo. While its last run is still open it does not fire
        -- again; it stays due and fires once that run is closed or
        -- abandoned. A run missed while nothing was ticking is due once,
        -- not once per missed slot, because the baseline moves to the
        -- moment it fires.
}

rule RunRoutineNow {
    when: OperatorRunsRoutine(owner?, name)

    let routine = the one active routine called name, of owner when given

    requires: exists routine
    requires: not routine.has_open_run

    ensures:
        let run = Memo.created(
            sender: dispatcher,
            recipient: routine.owner,
            routine: routine,
            subject: routine.name,
            body: routine.instructions,
            sent_at: now,
            status: unread,
            attempts: 0
        )
        routine.baseline = now
        routine.last_run = run

    @guidance
        -- relay routine run: the run goes out exactly as FireRoutines
        -- sends it, and the schedule counts from now. Two roles with a
        -- routine of one name need the owner named.
}

rule RetireOneOffRoutine {
    when: memo: Memo.created

    let routine = memo.routine

    requires: routine != null
    requires: routine.is_one_off

    ensures: routine.status = retired
}

-- Waking

rule WakeOnTick {
    when: DispatcherTicks(lost_wakes)

    for role in Roles where status = active and has_work and not is_busy and not is_paused and not is_running_away:
        ensures: DispatchedWakeSpawned(role: role)

    @guidance
        -- The tick then starts each wake in its own process, so a slow
        -- role holds up neither the others nor the next tick. A memo
        -- waiting out a retry delay is left out, and so is one hidden
        -- from a public role. Nobody is woken while their harness is
        -- paused.
}

rule StartDispatchedWake {
    when: DispatchedWakeSpawned(role, pid, pid_start)

    -- The state is looked at again when the spawned process gets
    -- there, so anything that changed since the tick refuses the wake.
    requires: role.status = active
    requires: not role.is_busy
    requires: not role.is_paused
    requires: not role.is_running_away
    requires: role.waiting_memos.count > 0

    ensures: Wake.created(
        role: role,
        memos: own_first(role.waiting_memos),   -- black box: see guidance
        resumes: fresh_or_interrupted(role),   -- black box: see guidance
        harness_name: role.harness.name,
        pid: pid,
        pid_start: pid_start,
        chat: false,
        started_at: now,
        status: running
    )
    ensures: role.interrupted_wake = null

    @guidance
        -- A dispatched wake carries only the memos that are not
        -- backing off. It carries on the interrupted wake, if there is
        -- one. If nothing is waiting any more, nothing is recorded.
        -- own_first: when any memo has no outside source (the
        -- operator's own, her verified replies, routines, roles' work),
        -- the wake takes only those, and the mailbox, GitHub and
        -- calendar memos wait for the next. A wake's work counts every
        -- memo it read as a source, so her request taken with a
        -- stranger's mail would read as drawn on it.
}

rule StartRequestedWake {
    when: WakeRequested(caller, role, note?, pid, pid_start)

    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.is_dispatcher
    requires: role.status = active
    requires: not role.is_busy
    requires: role.deliverable_memos.count > 0 or (note != null and note != "")

    ensures: Wake.created(
        role: role,
        memos: own_first(role.deliverable_memos),
        note: note,
        resumes: fresh_or_interrupted(role),
        harness_name: role.harness.name,
        pid: pid,
        pid_start: pid_start,
        chat: false,
        started_at: now,
        status: running
    )
    ensures: role.interrupted_wake = null

    @guidance
        -- A wake asked for by hand carries every open memo, including
        -- those backing off, and ignores the runaway guard and a paused
        -- harness, so it doubles as a way to try a harness early. In
        -- every other way it is an ordinary wake. With no open memos and
        -- no note it records nothing. It never carries a memo hidden
        -- from a public role.
}

rule OpenConversation {
    when: ConversationRequested(caller, role, note?, pid, pid_start)

    requires: caller.is_operator
    requires: role.status = active
    requires: role.open_conversations.count = 0

    ensures: Wake.created(
        role: role,
        memos: {},
        note: note,
        harness_name: role.harness.name,
        pid: pid,
        pid_start: pid_start,
        chat: true,
        started_at: now,
        status: running,
        turn: idle,
        turns: 0,
        turns_ended: 0,
        seen: 0,
        last_activity: now
    )

    @guidance
        -- A role keeps one conversation open at a time. A conversation
        -- holds the role only while a turn of it runs (StartTurn), so a
        -- conversation left open for days does not keep the dispatcher
        -- from the role's memos. It may open while a wake of the role
        -- works; its first turn waits for the wake to end. It carries
        -- no memos: what the role does with them there is up to the
        -- conversation, and nothing counts against them when it ends. It does not resume
        -- an interrupted wake and leaves it to be resumed later. It
        -- may open while a call of the role's waits for the operator,
        -- since it runs in a session of its own.
        -- Every session a conversation opens starts empty: the client
        -- can open and close sessions but not load, resume or list
        -- earlier ones, so no conversation carries on another's history
        -- or labels.
        -- A conversation runs over ACP, so any ACP client can hold one;
        -- the dashboard (bare relay) is one such client, on the operator's terminal.
        -- Its system prompt says when the conversation started, with the
        -- weekday, in the operator's time zone (a public role's too: the
        -- zone is not private), and points the role at the clock tool for
        -- the time after that and for date arithmetic.
}

rule StartTurn {
    when: TurnRequested(caller, wake, session)

    requires: caller.is_operator
    requires: wake.chat
    requires: wake.status = running
    requires: wake.turn = idle
    -- black box: an ACP session id, 1 to 128 letters, digits and . _ : -
    requires: is_session_id(session)
    requires: wake.role.working_wakes.count = 0

    ensures:
        wake.turn = running
        wake.turns = wake.turns + 1
        wake.turn_session = session
        wake.last_activity = now

    @guidance
        -- Each prompt the operator's client sends is a turn. relay's hub
        -- asks for it before the prompt reaches the agent. Refused
        -- because a wake of the role works, the prompt waits in the
        -- hub's queue, its turn shown as queued, and is asked for again
        -- whenever the log changes; it keeps its place if the client that
        -- sent it goes. Refused for any other reason, it is answered with
        -- relay's reason and the agent never sees it. A session takes one
        -- prompt at a time. The role takes one turn at a time: no turn
        -- starts while a wake works, and no wake starts while a turn
        -- runs.
}

rule EndTurn {
    when: TurnReported(wake, stop_reason)

    requires: wake.chat
    requires: wake.status = running
    requires: wake.turn = running

    ensures:
        wake.turn = idle
        wake.turns_ended = wake.turns
        wake.stop_reason = stop_reason   -- black box: one of the reasons a turn can end, else other
        wake.last_activity = now

    @guidance
        -- Only the dispatcher ends a turn, when the agent answers the
        -- prompt, and relay records it before the client sees the
        -- answer, so the client's next prompt finds the turn over.
        -- Telling relay of a turn that is not running records nothing
        -- and is not refused. A stop reason relay does not know is kept
        -- as other, so none of an agent's own text reaches the log.
}

rule SeeConversation {
    when: ConversationSeen(caller, wake, turn)

    requires: caller.is_operator
    requires: wake.chat
    requires: turn >= 1 and turn <= wake.turns

    ensures: wake.seen = if turn > wake.seen: turn else: wake.seen

    @guidance
        -- The operator has seen the conversation through that turn. A
        -- conversation has a reply the operator has not seen when a turn
        -- ended after the last one seen (turns_ended > seen). relay's
        -- roster (relay.roster) gives every client each active role with
        -- its title and labels, whether a wake of it works, and its open
        -- conversation's turn, turns and unread reply. It is read from the state
        -- alone, and relay roles shows it.
}

rule RunWake {
    when: wake: Wake.created

    ensures: HarnessStarted(wake: wake)

    @guidance
        -- The prompt tells the role who they are and what time it is,
        -- then gives each memo in full with its sender and how many
        -- earlier wakes left it open, and the note if there is one,
        -- then the role's last 3 journal entries (each cut at 600
        -- characters) and the topics of the facts that hold now with a
        -- count each. These are what the journal and facts tools would
        -- show the role with no arguments: only public items to a public
        -- role, and every item to any other. The wake's labels are those
        -- of everything in its prompts (AWakeStartsWithTheLabelsOfItsPrompts).
        -- A wake that resumes another continues that wake's session where
        -- the harness can and is told it was cut short. A conversation
        -- has no prompt and does not run headless: it runs over ACP, and
        -- the client sends each turn (StartTurn).
}

rule EndWake {
    when: WakeReported(wake, outcome, exit?, crashed, cut_short, session?, sessions?, said?, transcript?, resets_at?, labels?, usage?, cost_usd?, tools_error?, pins?)

    requires: wake.status = running
    requires: sessions = null or wake.chat

    ensures:
        wake.status = ended
        wake.ended_at = now
        wake.outcome = outcome
        wake.crashed = crashed
        wake.cut_short = cut_short
        wake.said = said
        wake.resets_at = resets_at
        wake.sessions = sessions ?? []
        wake.labels = labels ?? session_labels_bound(wake.role)       -- black box: see guidance
        wake.usage = usage
        wake.cost_usd = cost_usd
        wake.tools_error = if outcome = needs_attention and not wake.chat: tools_error else: null
        -- A conversation that ends during a turn ends the turn first,
        -- with the stop reason ended.
        wake.turn = idle
        wake.turns_ended = wake.turns

    @guidance
        -- Only the dispatcher ends wakes. Wakes end by the harness
        -- reporting, by the tick finding the process gone, or, for a
        -- conversation, when its ACP client goes away or relay is told
        -- to stop it. A wake reports
        -- the one session a later wake can resume. A conversation
        -- reports every session it used instead, so the log says which
        -- sessions a conversation used. With no labels reported, what the wake said carries every
        -- label anything in relay has, private, and the static labels
        -- of every tool the role is granted.
        -- A wake's usage and cost come from agentloop's outcome line. A
        -- conversation's cost is the sum of the last cost agentloop's
        -- usage_update gave for each of its sessions, and is null if any
        -- usage_update came without one. A usage or cost that is not
        -- one is dropped rather than refused, so a wake always ends.
}

rule InterruptedWakeIsKept {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    requires: wake.outcome != ran or wake.cut_short
    requires: not wake.chat

    ensures: wake.role.interrupted_wake = wake

    @guidance
        -- The next ordinary wake of the role carries on from this one.
        -- A wake cut short at its deadline still ran, so its memos are
        -- settled as for any wake that ran. If the role wrote no journal
        -- entry during it, the dispatcher writes one in the same step:
        -- the wake was cut short, when, and the ids and subjects of its
        -- memos. It carries those memos' labels, and is public only when
        -- the wake was a public session and every memo it quotes is.
        -- A conversation cut short is not resumed. Nor is a wake whose
        -- tool definition changed (TakeAChangedTool): its session pinned
        -- the old one.
}

-- The harness

rule HarnessRecovers {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    let harness = Harness{name: wake.harness_name}

    requires: wake.outcome = ran
    requires: harness.is_down

    ensures:
        harness.condition = available
        harness.paused_until = null
        harness.down_since = null
        harness.failed_tries = 0
        harness.operator_told = false

    @guidance
        -- Any run in which the role got to work shows the harness is
        -- fine, whatever became of the memos. Recovering records
        -- nothing when the harness was not down.
}

rule HarnessLimited {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    let harness = Harness{name: wake.harness_name}

    requires: wake.outcome = limited
    requires: wake.resets_at != null and wake.resets_at > now

    ensures:
        harness.condition = limited
        harness.paused_until = wake.resets_at
        harness.down_since = harness.down_since ?? now
}

rule HarnessLimitedWithoutAReset {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    let harness = Harness{name: wake.harness_name}

    requires: wake.outcome = limited
    requires: wake.resets_at = null or wake.resets_at <= now

    ensures:
        harness.condition = limited
        harness.paused_until = now + config.limit_probe_interval
        harness.down_since = harness.down_since ?? now

    @guidance
        -- Known to end, and usually known when. Nobody is told: the
        -- limit resets by itself and the work carries on. The count of
        -- failed tries is left as it was. A reset time that is not
        -- later than now is ignored and the probe interval is used.
}

rule HarnessUnreachable {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    let harness = Harness{name: wake.harness_name}
    let tries = harness.failed_tries + 1

    requires: wake.outcome = unreachable

    ensures:
        harness.condition = unreachable
        harness.failed_tries = tries
        harness.paused_until = now + retry_delay(tries)   -- black box: the same doubling wait as a memo
        harness.down_since = harness.down_since ?? now

    @guidance
        -- Expected to pass, but nobody knows when, so the harness is
        -- tried again at growing intervals for as long as it takes.
}

rule HarnessNeedsAttention {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    let harness = Harness{name: wake.harness_name}
    let tries = harness.failed_tries + 1

    requires: wake.outcome = needs_attention
    requires: wake.tools_error = null

    ensures:
        harness.condition = needs_attention
        harness.failed_tries = tries
        harness.paused_until = now + retry_delay(tries)
        harness.down_since = harness.down_since ?? now

    @guidance
        -- It will not pass until a person fixes it, such as signing
        -- in again. It is still tried at growing intervals, which is
        -- how the fix is noticed.
}

rule TellOperatorHarnessNeedsThem {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    let harness = Harness{name: wake.harness_name}

    requires: wake.outcome = needs_attention
    requires: wake.tools_error = null
    requires: not harness.operator_told

    ensures: Message.created(
        origin: harness_needs_attention,
        kind: alert,
        urgency: high,
        subject: "relay needs you before it can work",
        sections: [needs_attention_text(wake)],   -- black box: what it said, and that nothing was dropped
        harness: harness,
        created_at: now,
        deliveries: route(this, now)
    )
    ensures: harness.operator_told = true

    @guidance
        -- At once, and once per outage: the flag is cleared only when
        -- a run gets to work. A failure on this machine (agentloop did
        -- not start, or no such harness) is told as one, with what it
        -- said and that nothing changes until it is fixed here; only a
        -- model service's refusal is told as the service's. relay status
        -- shows what it said beside the harness.
}

rule ResolveAlerts {
    when: HarnessRecovers or SourcePolled or PublicRoleRunsAgain or ToolWorksAgain

    ensures: for alert in Messages where kind = alert and not resolved
                 and is_about_the_trouble_that_ended:
        alert.resolved = now

    @guidance
        -- harness_needs_attention and harness_unreachable for that
        -- harness, ingest_failing for that source,
        -- public_role_cannot_run for that role, and tool_broken for that
        -- tool. relay ready, and the client's ready view, leave a
        -- resolved alert out.
}

rule ToolNotSetUp {
    when: ToolCallFailed(tool, error)

    requires: setup_problem(error) != null   -- webtool's search key command failed
    requires: not tool.broken

    ensures: tool.broken = setup_problem(error)
    ensures: Message.created(
        origin: tool_broken,
        kind: alert,
        urgency: normal,
        subject: "Web search isn't set up yet",
        sections: [how_to_fix(setup_problem(error))],
        created_at: now,
        deliveries: route(this, now)
    )

    @guidance
        -- Once, by relay, in plain words with the command that fixes it,
        -- and with no outside label: it is a setting on this machine.
        -- The role is told not to report it. The next call that works
        -- clears tool.broken and resolves the alert (ToolWorksAgain).
        -- Nothing reruns the work it stopped, so each request of the
        -- operator's own that the failing session carried is named,
        -- once, with "ask again once the key is in": in this alert, or,
        -- when the tool is broken already, in a short one of its own.
}

rule SettingNamesNoRole {
    when: DispatcherTicks(lost_wakes)

    let problems = role_name_problems(config, active_roles)
    requires: problems != told_misnamed

    ensures: told_misnamed = problems
    ensures: for alert in Messages where origin = settings_misnamed and not resolved:
        alert.resolved = now
    ensures:
        if problems.any:
            Message.created(origin: settings_misnamed, kind: alert, urgency: normal,
                            subject: "relay.edn names a role that isn't there",
                            sections: [problems], created_at: now, deliveries: route(this, now))

    @guidance
        -- role_name_problems: config.dead_letter_handler, and
        -- serve.websocket.default_role when there is a websocket, each
        -- when it names no active role while some role is active, with
        -- the likely main role (the first house role that may add
        -- roles) to set instead. An install made when the main role
        -- was hub otherwise loses dead letters to the operator, and
        -- phone sessions, without a word. relay status shows the same
        -- lines.
}

-- MCP tools that could not be set up

rule ToolsUnavailable {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    let role = wake.role
    let tries = role.tools_failed_tries + 1

    requires: wake.tools_error != null
    requires: not takes_changed_tool(wake)   -- black box: as TakeAChangedTool decides it

    ensures:
        role.tools_unavailable_session = wake.session
        role.tools_failed_tries = tries
        role.tools_retry_at = now + retry_delay(tries)

    @guidance
        -- agentloop ran nothing: a server did not start, or a tool's
        -- definition is not the one the settings' digest pins. No model
        -- was called, so the harness is not paused and other roles go
        -- on. The wake is kept to be resumed (InterruptedWakeIsKept)
        -- and its memos count no attempt. The role is tried again after
        -- a doubling wait, in the same session. relay never moves the
        -- settings' digest, since it is the operator's own pin: she
        -- fixes that in the settings.
}

rule TakeAChangedTool {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    let tool = Tool{name: wake.tools_error.tool}

    requires: wake.tools_error.pinned != null and wake.tools_error.got != null
    requires: tool.is_mcp                                -- black box
    requires: configured_digest(tool) = null             -- black box: the tool's :digest in the settings
    requires: tool.accepted_tool_digest != wake.tools_error.got
    requires: wake.role.changed_tool != tool

    ensures: tool.accepted_tool_digest = wake.tools_error.got
    ensures: wake.role.changed_tool = tool
    ensures: Message.created(
        origin: tool_changed,
        kind: note,
        urgency: normal,
        subject: tool.name + " changed",
        sections: [tool_changed_text(wake)],   -- black box: relay uses the new version, and the role starts afresh with it
        role: wake.role,
        created_at: now,
        deliveries: route(this, now)
    )

    @guidance
        -- The server now describes the tool differently from the
        -- definition the session pinned. agentloop refused it before
        -- any model saw it. relay takes the new definition and tells
        -- the operator once: a second session stopped by the same change
        -- finds the new digest already accepted and records nothing.
        -- The role is not kept to be resumed, since its session pinned
        -- the old definition, and its next wake starts a new session
        -- with its open memos. Every other role's next request names the
        -- new digest too.
}

rule ChangedToolAgain {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    let tool = Tool{name: wake.tools_error.tool}
    let role = wake.role
    let tries = role.tools_failed_tries + 1

    requires: wake.tools_error.pinned != null and wake.tools_error.got != null
    requires: tool.is_mcp                                -- black box
    requires: configured_digest(tool) = null             -- black box
    requires: tool.accepted_tool_digest != wake.tools_error.got
    requires: role.changed_tool = tool

    ensures:
        tool.accepted_tool_digest = wake.tools_error.got
        role.tools_unavailable_session = wake.session
        role.tools_failed_tries = tries
        role.tools_retry_at = now + retry_delay(tries)

    @guidance
        -- A server whose description carries a timestamp, a counter or
        -- a random id differs on every connect. relay still takes each
        -- new definition, so a server that settles works at the next
        -- try, but waits a doubling time first and tells the operator
        -- nothing more: one message per streak, and no session
        -- started on every tick.
}

rule TellOperatorToolsUnavailable {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    requires: wake.tools_error != null
    requires: not takes_changed_tool(wake)
    requires: wake.role.tools_unavailable_session = null

    ensures: Message.created(
        origin: tools_unavailable,
        kind: alert,
        urgency: normal,
        subject: "Some work could not start: a connection failed",
        sections: [tools_unavailable_text(wake)],     -- black box: what agentloop said, and relay wake or the settings' digest
        role: wake.role,
        created_at: now,
        deliveries: route(this, now)
    )

    @guidance
        -- Once per outage. The message carries the session's
        -- labels.
}

rule RememberToolDefinitions {
    when: WakeReported(wake, outcome, exit?, crashed, cut_short, session?, sessions?, said?, transcript?, resets_at?, labels?, usage?, cost_usd?, tools_error?, pins?)

    requires: not wake.chat

    for tool in Tools where pins[tool.name] != null and accepted_tool_digest = null:
        ensures: tool.accepted_tool_digest = pins[tool.name]

    @guidance
        -- pins are the digests agentloop's session pinned in this run,
        -- from its pins entries. Trust on first use, as SSH's
        -- known_hosts: only a tool with no accepted digest takes one.
}

rule ToolsAvailableAgain {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    requires: wake.outcome = ran
    requires: not wake.chat
    requires: wake.role.tools_unavailable_session != null

    ensures:
        wake.role.tools_unavailable_session = null
        wake.role.tools_retry_at = null
        wake.role.tools_failed_tries = 0
}

rule ChangedToolStreakEnds {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    requires: wake.outcome = ran
    requires: not wake.chat

    ensures: wake.role.changed_tool = null
}

rule ConnectRemoteServer {
    when: ConnectRequested(caller, name, chosen)

    requires: caller.is_operator
    -- The operator signed in at the server's own sign-in page.

    for tool in chosen where on:
        ensures: tool.accepted_tool_digest = tool.digest_listed

    @guidance
        -- relay connect <name> <url>. Each tool is proposed read and on
        -- when the server says it only reads, and edit and off otherwise,
        -- with labels private and contaminated; one whose name says it
        -- deletes starts off too. The operator turns a tool on, as edit,
        -- in the connection file once she has checked it changes only
        -- her own things. relay shows her the tools and what each may
        -- do, then writes the file.
        -- The sign-in talks to one authorization server, which must name
        -- itself in every answer if it says it does (RFC 9207), and
        -- otherwise keep its endpoints on its own origin; each sign-in
        -- has a redirect of its own.
        -- Pinning at connect means no definition is taken on trust, and
        -- connecting again replaces what was pinned before. A tool that
        -- is off is not pinned and no role can have it.
}

rule TellOperatorOfLongOutage {
    when: DispatcherTicks(lost_wakes)

    for harness in Harnesses where condition = unreachable and not operator_told and down_since != null and down_since + config.outage_patience <= now:
        ensures: Message.created(
            origin: harness_unreachable,
            kind: alert,
            urgency: high,
            subject: "The model service has been unreachable since " + harness.down_since,
            sections: ["Work waits, and nothing has been dropped. It carries on by itself once the service is back."],
            harness: harness,
            created_at: now,
            deliveries: route(this, now)
        )
        ensures: harness.operator_told = true

    @guidance
        -- One message per outage. Reported by the tick, not by the
        -- failing wake, so it takes the first tick after the patience
        -- has run out.
}

-- Retrying and giving up

rule RetryMemoLater {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    requires: wake.outcome = ran   -- the harness's failures fail no memo

    for memo in wake.memos:
        let attempt = memo.attempts + 1

        requires: memo.status = unread
        requires: attempt < config.max_attempts

        ensures:
            memo.attempts = attempt
            memo.retry_at = now + retry_delay(attempt)   -- black box: see guidance

    @guidance
        -- A memo the wake carried and left open has failed once more,
        -- however the harness exited, and a wake the tick found lost
        -- counts too. retry_delay is retry_base doubled for each attempt
        -- after the first, and never more than retry_ceiling. Nobody is
        -- told: a failure that will be retried does not need anyone.
        -- A conversation carries no memos, so it counts against nothing.
}

rule AbandonMemo {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    requires: wake.outcome = ran

    for memo in wake.memos:
        let attempt = memo.attempts + 1

        requires: memo.status = unread
        requires: attempt >= config.max_attempts

        ensures: memo.attempts = attempt
        ensures: memo.retry_at = null
        ensures: MemoDeadLettered(
            memo: memo,
            reason: never_closed,
            transcript_tail: wake.said,
            wake: wake
        )
}

rule EndLostWakes {
    when: DispatcherTicks(lost_wakes)

    for wake in lost_wakes where status = running and not chat:
        ensures: WakeReported(
            wake: wake,
            outcome: ran,
            crashed: true,
            cut_short: false,
            said: "The process running this wake disappeared."
        )

    for wake in lost_wakes where status = running and chat:
        ensures: WakeReported(
            wake: wake,
            outcome: ran,
            crashed: false,
            cut_short: false,
            said: "The conversation's client went away without letting relay record the end."
        )

    @guidance
        -- A wake whose process is gone (found by pid and the time
        -- the process started, so that a later process that was given
        -- the same pid does not count) ended without saying how. It
        -- counts against its memos like a crash, so a memo that kills
        -- its runner every time is still dead-lettered in the end.
        -- A conversation carries no memos, and its process belongs to
        -- its ACP client. A client may close it by killing it outright:
        -- Zed sends SIGKILL to the agent server's whole process group,
        -- which relay cannot handle. So a lost conversation is recorded
        -- as its client going away, not as a crash.
}

rule TripRunawayGuard {
    when: DispatcherTicks(lost_wakes)

    for role in Roles where status = active and has_work and not is_busy and is_running_away:
        requires:
            role.guard_reported_at = null
            or role.guard_reported_at + config.runaway_window <= now

        ensures:
            role.guard_reported_at = now
            Message.created(
                origin: runaway_guard_tripped,
                kind: alert,
                urgency: high,
                subject: "relay paused work that kept restarting",
                sections: ["The work is waiting and nothing was dropped."],
                about: role,
                created_at: now,
                deliveries: route(this, now)
            )

    @guidance
        -- The role is not woken by the dispatcher again until the
        -- window has room. Their work waits; none of it is dropped. The
        -- operator is told once per window.
}

-- Messages to the operator

rule TellOperator {
    -- tell_operator: a house role tells the operator something. It
    -- gives the content and the urgency; it never chooses a medium, an
    -- address or a recipient.
    when: TellOperator(role, subject, sections, urgency, in_reply_to)

    requires: role.status = active
    requires: not role.is_public
    requires: length(subject) <= config.max_subject_length

    @guidance
        -- The subject is one line. in_reply_to names a message relay
        -- sent, or nothing.

    ensures: Message.created(
        origin: told,
        kind: if in_reply_to = null: note else: reply,
        urgency: urgency ?? normal,
        subject: subject,
        sections: sections,
        in_reply_to: in_reply_to,
        about: role,
        created_at: now,
        deliveries: route(this, now)
    )

    @guidance
        -- A public role reports back by memo instead. The message
        -- carries the labels of what the session read.
}

-- route(message, now) is a pure function of relay.edn's :messages:
-- every configured channel a matching route names (a route matches on
-- its :kinds and :urgencies, each optional), due now, or at the next
-- :digest-at for a channel that only :at :digest routes name. Quiet
-- hours hold any delivery of a message that is not high urgency until
-- they end; high urgency goes at once.

rule DeliverMessage {
    when: message: Message.created
    for delivery in message.deliveries where delivery.due <= now:
        ensures: DeliveryMade(message, delivery.channel)

    @guidance
        -- Messages are recorded first, as part of the same append as
        -- whatever caused them, and delivered after it.
}

rule DeliverWhatIsDue {
    when: DispatcherTicks(lost_wakes)

    for (channel, messages) in due_deliveries(now):
        ensures: DeliveryMade(messages, channel)

    @guidance
        -- The tick delivers what was held for quiet hours or the
        -- digest and has come due, what a process recorded and stopped
        -- before delivering (pending over two minutes), and what failed
        -- and is due again. What comes due together on one channel goes
        -- as one push or one email.
}

rule DeliverySucceeded {
    when: DeliverySucceeded(messages, channel)

    for d in Deliveries where d.channel = channel and d.message in messages:
        ensures: d.status = delivered
}

rule DeliveryFailed {
    when: DeliveryFailed(messages, channel, error)

    let tried = Deliveries where channel = channel and message in messages
    let attempt = tried.map(d => d.attempts).max + 1

    for d in tried:
        ensures:
            d.status = failed
            d.attempts = attempt
            d.retry_at = if attempt < config.delivery_attempts: now + retry_delay(attempt) else: null

    @guidance
        -- The wait doubles from retry_base up to retry_ceiling, as for a
        -- memo, and relay gives up after delivery_attempts tries, or at
        -- once when relay.edn no longer has the channel.
}

-- What comes in from outside (relay.ingest)

rule IngestRecord {
    -- An ingest source in relay.edn's :ingest (a POP3 mailbox, GitHub
    -- repositories, a calendar feed) was polled by the tick, and what
    -- it found is recorded. Only relay.edn says what to fetch.
    when: IngestPolled(source, items, keys, cursor)

    requires: source.to.status = active

    for item in items where seen(source, item.key) != item.version:
        ensures: Memo.sent(to: source.to, from: dispatcher,
                           labels: {contaminated, source_label(source, item)})

    @guidance
        -- One memo per mail; per repository, one for every 50 items a
        -- poll returned, all recorded at once since the GitHub cursor is
        -- past them; one per calendar per poll, listing at most 50 new
        -- or changed and 50 removed events. A calendar answer that is
        -- not a whole VCALENDAR is a failed poll, never a removal of
        -- every event. What was seen at the
        -- same version is never recorded again, so two ticks that poll
        -- at once record it once. relay never deletes from the mailbox.
}

rule OperatorMail {
    -- A mail is the operator's only when verified: one From naming the
    -- :to of an email channel, exactly one Authentication-Results with
    -- the source's :authserv-id, and that one says dkim=pass for the
    -- operator's domain. Every header line ends CRLF, and so does the
    -- blank line that ends them. A mail that names the operator's
    -- address and is not verified is labelled mail:unverified-operator,
    -- never with that address.
    when: IngestPolled(source, items, keys, cursor)

    for mail in items where verified(mail):
        if answers(mail) != null:
            ensures: MessageReplied(answers(mail), channel, text)   -- ReplyToAMessage sends the memo
        else:
            ensures: Memo.sent(to: source.to, from: operator, labels: {})

    @guidance
        -- answers(mail) is the message whose Message-ID relay made
        -- (at an agent domain, with the message's creation time) that
        -- In-Reply-To or References names. The memo goes to the role
        -- that sent that message. A mail that is not verified is from
        -- outside, as any other, and joins no thread.
}

invariant NoUnverifiedMailIsTrusted {
    for m in Memos where m.from = operator and m.sent_by = dispatcher:
        verified(m.mail)
}

rule IngestFailing {
    when: IngestFailed(source, error)
    ensures: source.failing = error
    if config.daily_note_at = null and now - source.failing_since >= config.outage_patience and not source.told:
        ensures: Message.created(kind: alert, origin: ingest_failing)

    @guidance
        -- With a daily note, a failing source is listed in each note
        -- until it works (MakeDailyNote), and sends no alert of its own.
}

-- Spend

-- relay status shows this week's WeekSpend: each role's spend, the
-- total, and the wakes that ran without a cost. Below it is the total of
-- each of the four weeks before. It is worked out from the wakes when
-- asked, and nothing is recorded for it. A wake belongs to the week it
-- ended in, so one that ends at Monday 00:00 belongs to the new week.
-- Spend is shown and warned of, nothing more: relay never stops or
-- slows a role for what it costs.

rule WarnOfSpend {
    when: wake: Wake.status transitions_to ended

    let week = week_of(now)                              -- black box: the WeekSpend holding now
    let total = week.cost_usd.values.sum
    let told = (Messages where origin = budget_reached and week = week.week).map(n => n.percent).max ?? 0
    let percent = if total >= config.weekly_budget: 100
                  else if total * 100 >= config.weekly_budget * 80: 80
                  else: 0

    requires: config.weekly_budget != null
    requires: wake.cost_usd != null
    requires: percent > told

    ensures: Message.created(
        origin: budget_reached,
        kind: alert,
        urgency: normal,
        subject: if percent = 100: "relay has spent its weekly budget"
               else: "relay has spent 80% of its weekly budget",
        sections: [spend_text(total, week.week, config.weekly_budget)],   -- black box: the total, the week and the budget
        week: week.week,
        percent: percent,
        created_at: now,
        deliveries: route(this, now)
    )

    @guidance
        -- The total is every role's spend this week together. The
        -- operator is told once when it reaches 80% of the budget and
        -- once when it reaches 100%, at most once each a week. A wake
        -- that takes the total past both at once tells only 100%: one
        -- warning that the budget is spent says all two would. Only a
        -- wake with a cost can move the total, so only such a wake is
        -- checked. A new week starts with nothing told.
}

-- Reviewing a week

-- relay week reports a window of the log: each interruption (a harness
-- that needs the operator, work given up to the operator) from the event
-- that asked to the event that answered, the messages sent, each role's wakes and what they
-- cost, health checks on each wake, and the operator's flags. relay
-- traces exports the same wakes as OpenTelemetry spans, holding no
-- content. Both are worked out from the log and the run files when
-- asked, and record nothing.

rule FlagWake {
    when: WakeFlagRequested(caller, wake, value, note?)

    requires: caller.is_operator
    requires: wake != null

    ensures: wake.flags = wake.flags + WakeFlag(value: value, note: note, at: now)

    @guidance
        -- relay flag <wake> good|bad [note] marks a wake or a
        -- conversation to find it later. No role sees it. An id that names no wake is
        -- refused.
}

-- The daily note

rule MakeDailyNote {
    when: DispatcherTicks(lost_wakes)

    let today = local_date(now)                              -- black box: now's date in the time zone
    let due_at = at_local(today, config.daily_note_at)       -- black box: a time a clock change skips moves forward by the gap
    let last = DailyNotes.max_by(n => n.date)
    let since = if last = null: now - 1.day else: last.created_at
    let flagged = RecipeChanges.where(c =>
        c.created_after(since) and c.actor not in {operator, dispatcher} and outside(c.sources))
    let parts = NoteParts.where(p => p.written_after(since))
        .map(p => p.without(Dismissed))
    let github = GitHubNews                                  -- items people opened since the last note
    let problems = IngestSources.where(s => s.failing)

    requires: config.daily_note_at != null
    requires: now >= due_at
    requires: last = null or last.date < today

    ensures: DailyNote.created(date: today, sent: flagged.any or parts.any or github.any or problems.any,
                               flagged: flagged, created_at: now)
    ensures: GitHubNews = []
    ensures:
        if flagged.any or parts.any or github.any or problems.any:
            Message.created(
                origin: daily_note,
                kind: digest,
                urgency: normal,
                subject: "Daily note for " + today,
                sections: [flagged, problems, ahead, grants, github, learned],
                numbered: numbered(flagged, parts),
                date: today,
                created_at: now,
                deliveries: route(this, now)
            )

    @guidance
        -- outside(sources): any source (ProvenanceIsWhatAWakeReadDirectly).
        -- A change the operator asked for in a wake that read nothing
        -- from outside is hers, and quiet. relay works out the flagged
        -- section in code; no model writes it or can leave a change out
        -- of it (decision 14). Each says what changed in one line,
        -- where the outside text came from by name ("the web page
        -- office-holidays.html"), a line of what it now says, and how
        -- to undo it (reply "revert N"; relay revert N takes the same
        -- N). A new or removed role is listed with the reason it cannot
        -- be undone and no number. Past 40 it counts the rest, which
        -- relay changes lists with their handles. problems names each
        -- ingest source that is failing. github lists, by repository,
        -- the items people opened since the last note, each with a link
        -- relay builds from the repository and number, then what the
        -- role wrote for github. The other parts are what the note's
        -- role wrote with daily_note_write: ahead, grants, learned.
        -- Every part but the flagged and problems sections is there
        -- each day, saying so when it has nothing; github only when a
        -- repository is watched.
        -- Suggestions in ahead and grants are numbered so the operator
        -- can drop one. No role, tool, label or class is named in the
        -- text. A day's note is due from its time until the day ends;
        -- a day with no tick past its time has none. relay note now
        -- makes the day's note at once when the day has none yet, or
        -- only one that was not sent; it records nothing when there is
        -- nothing to say, so an empty note never uses up the day.
}

rule RecordRecipeChange {
    when: an event writes a skill doc, a routine, a role's note or a role
    ensures: RecipeChange.created(what, change, owner, name, actor, labels, sources, before, peek)

    @guidance
        -- Folded from the event and the state before it, so it can always
        -- be rebuilt from the log. peek is the first substantive line the
        -- change adds: not a heading or a skill's "Use when:" line,
        -- unless it adds nothing else.
        -- A listing of routines or skills (relay routines, relay status,
        -- relay docs) ends the line of one whose latest version has
        -- sources with a short mark of what kind of thing they were:
        -- "(from a web page)", "(from a mail and a web page)", or
        -- "(from outside)" for more kinds or none known.
}

rule WriteNotePart {
    when: RoleCalls(role, daily_note_write, part, items)
    requires: role = config.daily_note_role
    ensures: NotePart.replaced(part, items.without(Dismissed), labels: session.labels)
}

rule RevertChange {
    when: OperatorReverts(change)
    -- relay revert N [note], _relay/messages/act on a revert item, or
    -- a reply "revert N" to the note from any channel (ReplyToAMessage).
    -- N is the note's number for the change. A change no note numbered
    -- (past the note's 40, after the latest note, quiet, or the
    -- operator's own) goes by its handle in relay changes, c and its
    -- place among all changes: relay revert cK. The log's own number is
    -- never shown to the operator.
    requires: not change.reverted
    requires: change.what != role or change.change = changed
    requires: change.undo_of = null
    ensures: change.reverted = true
    ensures: what change replaced is put back, with the labels of the
        text it restores; what it made new is removed

    @guidance
        -- When change.prior was undone too, the undo goes back past it
        -- to what that one replaced, and so on. Undoing several changes
        -- to one thing, in any order, ends at the version before all of
        -- them, never at text one of them wrote.
}

rule DismissSuggestion {
    when: OperatorDismisses(note, n)
    -- relay dismiss <n>, _relay/messages/act on a dismiss item, or a
    -- reply "not N" from any channel (or "not this one" when the note
    -- has one).
    ensures: Dismissed.created(keys: note.numbered[n].keys)

    @guidance
        -- Later parts drop any suggestion with one of its keys, and the
        -- writer is shown what was dropped (daily_note_draft).
}

rule AnnounceGitHubItems {
    when: DispatcherTicks(lost_wakes)
    let news = items an ingest poll found new, opened by a person (user type User, not a bot)
    requires: news.any
    requires: config.daily_note_at = null
    ensures: Message.created(origin: github_news, kind: note, urgency: low, sections: news.by_repository)

    @guidance
        -- Nothing about a new item is urgent. With a daily note, the
        -- items wait for it (MakeDailyNote). A failing ingest source
        -- likewise goes into the note rather than an alert.
}

-- Tools

rule RunTool {
    when: ToolCallRequested(caller, tool, arguments)

    requires: caller.role != null and caller.role.status = active
    requires: tool in caller.role.offered_tools

    ensures: ToolRan(role: caller.role, tool: tool, arguments: arguments)

    @guidance
        -- What a tool does is the command it stands for, decided in the
        -- ordinary way with the role as the caller. A refusal comes back
        -- to the role as text, so it can read why and adjust.
}

-- The agent's calendar

rule AddCalendarEvent {
    when: CalendarAddRequested(caller, title, start, end?, location?, description?)

    -- The calendar is the agent's own. The operator and the dispatcher
    -- never write it, so the feed holds only what a role wrote, and a
    -- public role has none. relay never writes the operator's calendar.
    requires: caller is Role and not caller.is_public
    requires: title != "" and title.length <= 200
    requires: end = null or end > start
    requires: year(start) in 1970..9999
    requires: CalendarEvent.where(not is_removed).count < config.max_calendar_events

    ensures: CalendarEventVersion.created(
        event: CalendarEvent.created(),
        change: added,
        recorded_at: now,
        actor: caller,
        title: title,
        start: start,
        end: end ?? start + 1.hour,
        location: location,
        description: description
    )
}

rule UpdateCalendarEvent {
    when: CalendarUpdateRequested(caller, event, title?, start?, end?, location?, description?, why?)

    requires: caller is Role and not caller.is_public
    requires: not event.is_removed
    requires: the new version differs from event.current
    requires: the new end is after the new start

    ensures: CalendarEventVersion.created(
        event: event,
        change: changed,
        recorded_at: now,
        actor: caller,
        title: title ?? event.current.title,
        start: start ?? event.current.start,
        end: end ?? event.current.end,
        location: location ?? event.current.location,
        description: description ?? event.current.description,
        why: why
    )

    @guidance
        -- An empty location or description clears it. A new start at or
        -- after the old end needs a new end too.
}

rule RemoveCalendarEvent {
    when: CalendarRemoveRequested(caller, event, why?)

    requires: caller is Role and not caller.is_public
    requires: not event.is_removed

    ensures: CalendarEventVersion.created(
        event: event,
        change: removed,
        recorded_at: now,
        actor: caller,
        title: event.current.title,
        start: event.current.start,
        end: event.current.end,
        location: event.current.location,
        description: event.current.description,
        why: why
    )
}

rule ServeCalendarFeed {
    when: CalendarFeedRequested(request)

    -- The feed is served on the WebSocket listener only (127.0.0.1, behind
    -- the operator's tailnet), to the feed's own token given as a bearer
    -- token or as ?token= in the URL, and to no request with a foreign
    -- Origin. It lists every event; a removed one stays as STATUS:CANCELLED
    -- for 30 days and is then dropped. Times are UTC, DTSTAMP is the time of
    -- the event's last change, and lines are folded at 75 octets. An
    -- all-day event is DATE values: its first day and the day after its
    -- last. The feed's token is HMAC-SHA256 of a fixed text keyed with
    -- the listener's token: it opens the feed and nothing else, and the
    -- listener's token does not open the feed. relay calendar url prints
    -- the URL with it.
    requires: request.path = "/calendar.ics" and request.method = GET
    requires: request.token = feed_token(config.serve.websocket.token)
}

-- Organizing files

rule MoveFiles {
    when: FilesMoveRequested(caller, moves)

    -- relay's own code makes the moves on the host; the model and the
    -- container never touch the disk. Every move is checked before any
    -- is made, and one refused move refuses the call.
    requires: caller is Role and not caller.is_public and caller.files != []
    requires: moves.count in 1..100
    requires: every folder in caller.files, as its real path, passes the
        shell's place and identity checks   -- never a secret, the home directory, the data directory or the data volume
    requires: for m in moves:
        real(m.from) and real(m.to) lie inside one of caller.files
        and m.from is a file or a folder holding no link
        and m.from is not one of caller.files and holds none of them
        and nothing exists at m.to
        and m.from and m.to are on one disk
    requires: no two moves touch the same path or one inside another

    ensures: MoveCall.created(actor: caller, moves: moves, status: moving)
    ensures: each move is made with an atomic rename, the folders its
        target needs made and recorded, then the call is moved

    @guidance
        -- Both events carry the session's labels and private, since
        -- the paths are the operator's.
}

rule UndoMove {
    when: MoveUndoRequested(operator, call)

    requires: call.status = moved
    requires: for step in call.done where not step.index in call.undone:
        fingerprint(call.moves[step.index].to) = step.fingerprint
        and nothing exists at call.moves[step.index].from
        and the folders above both are where they were, links resolved

    ensures: each step is renamed back, in reverse order
    ensures: each folder the steps made is removed when it is empty
    ensures: call.undone = every done index

    @guidance
        -- When a requirement fails, undo says what changed and touches
        -- nothing. A folder it made that holds something new is kept.
        -- The operator asks for it with relay undo or, from the ready
        -- view, _relay/undo; both run the same code. Each call is a move
        -- item in the ready view, offering undo while a step is left to
        -- undo or relay never finished the call.
}

-- Knowledge: facts

rule AddFact {
    when: FactAddRequested(caller, topic?, text, valid_from?, valid_to?)

    requires: topic = null or is_usable_topic(topic)   -- black box: lower case words joined by hyphens, / between levels, at most 100 characters
    requires: text != ""
    requires: text.length <= config.max_fact_length
    requires: valid_from = null or valid_to = null or valid_to > valid_from

    ensures:
        let fact = Fact.created()
        FactVersion.created(
            fact: fact,
            change: added,
            recorded_at: now,
            actor: caller,
            topic: topic,
            text: text,
            valid_from: valid_from,
            valid_to: valid_to
        )

    @guidance
        -- Times are an ISO instant, a date or a date and time in the
        -- operator's time zone. A date is midnight. Anything else is
        -- refused.
}

rule SupersedeFact {
    when: FactSupersedeRequested(caller, fact, topic?, text, valid_from?, valid_to?)

    let old = fact.current
    -- The change begins now unless said otherwise.
    let from = valid_from ?? now

    requires: not fact.is_retracted
    requires: not fact.is_superseded
    requires: topic = null or is_usable_topic(topic)
    requires: old.valid_from = null or from > old.valid_from
    requires: old.valid_to = null or from <= old.valid_to
    requires: text != ""
    requires: text.length <= config.max_fact_length
    requires: valid_to = null or valid_to > from

    ensures:
        -- The new state of affairs is a new fact.
        let successor = Fact.created(supersedes: fact)
        FactVersion.created(
            fact: successor,
            change: added,
            recorded_at: now,
            actor: caller,
            topic: topic ?? old.topic,
            text: text,
            valid_from: from,
            valid_to: valid_to
        )
        -- The old fact gets a new version that ends where the change begins.
        FactVersion.created(
            fact: fact,
            change: superseded,
            recorded_at: now,
            actor: caller,
            topic: old.topic,
            text: old.text,
            valid_from: old.valid_from,
            valid_to: from,
            superseded_by: successor
        )

    @guidance
        -- The world changed. Use correct when the record was wrong. A
        -- fact is superseded once; supersede the newest one. The change
        -- must come after the fact began to hold (if it was wrong from
        -- the start, correct it) and not after it had already stopped
        -- (add a new fact instead). A change at the moment the fact
        -- stopped is allowed.
}

rule CorrectFact {
    when: FactCorrectRequested(caller, fact, why, topic?, text?, valid_from?, valid_to?)

    let cur = fact.current
    -- "open" clears a bound; a bound not given is unchanged.
    let new_from = corrected_bound(valid_from, cur.valid_from)   -- black box: open gives null, nothing gives the current
    let new_to = corrected_bound(valid_to, cur.valid_to)

    requires: not fact.is_retracted
    requires: why != ""
    requires: new_from = null or new_to = null or new_to > new_from
    -- A blank text or topic means unchanged.
    requires: topic = null or topic = "" or is_usable_topic(topic)
    requires: text = null or text?.length <= config.max_fact_length
    -- It must change something.
    requires: (topic ?? cur.topic) != cur.topic or (text ?? cur.text) != cur.text
        or new_from != cur.valid_from or new_to != cur.valid_to

    ensures: FactVersion.created(
        fact: fact,
        change: corrected,
        recorded_at: now,
        actor: caller,
        topic: topic ?? cur.topic,
        text: text ?? cur.text,
        valid_from: new_from,
        valid_to: new_to,
        why: why,
        superseded_by: cur.superseded_by
    )

    @guidance
        -- The record was wrong, not the world. This writes a new
        -- version of the same fact, so asking what was known before
        -- the correction still gives the old answer.
}

rule RetractFact {
    when: FactRetractRequested(caller, fact, why)

    let cur = fact.current

    requires: not fact.is_retracted
    requires: why != ""
    -- In the middle of a chain of changes, restoring the fact it replaced
    -- would leave that fact and its successor's both holding.
    requires: fact.supersedes = null or cur.superseded_by = null

    ensures: FactVersion.created(
        fact: fact,
        change: retracted,
        recorded_at: now,
        actor: caller,
        topic: cur.topic,
        text: cur.text,
        valid_from: cur.valid_from,
        valid_to: cur.valid_to,
        why: why,
        superseded_by: cur.superseded_by
    )

    @guidance
        -- A retraction is a correction saying the fact was never true.
        -- The fact is kept and answers for what relay knew before, and
        -- no longer holds, or appears in any listing, after.
}

rule RetractionUndoesItsChange {
    when: version: FactVersion.created

    let gone = version.fact
    let old = gone.supersedes

    requires: version.change = retracted
    requires: old != null
    requires: old.current.superseded_by = gone

    -- The change never happened, so the fact it replaced is put back as
    -- it was before the supersession, own end included.
    ensures: FactVersion.created(
        fact: old,
        change: corrected,
        recorded_at: now,
        actor: version.actor,
        topic: old.current.topic,
        text: old.current.text,
        valid_from: old.current.valid_from,
        valid_to: version_before_supersession(old, gone).valid_to,   -- black box
        why: "The fact that superseded it was retracted.",
        superseded_by: null
    )

    @guidance
        -- Retracting a fact that superseded another restores the old
        -- one, as one event with the retraction. Only the fact it
        -- directly replaced is restored. What relay knew before the
        -- retraction is still answered as it was.
}

-- Knowledge: notes, journal, docs

rule WriteNote {
    when: NoteWriteRequested(caller, owner, name, text)

    -- A role writes its own notes. The operator names the role. The
    -- dispatcher has none.
    requires: owner.status = active
    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.role = owner
    requires: is_usable_note_name(name)   -- black box: lower case letters, digits and hyphens, at most 48 characters
    requires: text != ""
    requires: text.length <= config.max_note_length
    requires: not exists Note{owner: owner, name: name}

    ensures: Note.created(owner: owner, name: name, text: text, written_at: now)
}

rule RewriteNote {
    when: NoteWriteRequested(caller, owner, name, text)

    let note = Note{owner: owner, name: name}

    requires: exists note
    requires: owner.status = active
    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.role = owner
    requires: text != ""
    requires: text.length <= config.max_note_length
    -- Writing the same text again records nothing.
    requires: text != note.text

    ensures:
        note.text = text
        note.written_at = now

    @guidance
        -- Writing a note replaces it. Notes go into the prompt of every
        -- wake of their role, which is why they are short. Longer
        -- content belongs in a doc.
}

rule RemoveNote {
    when: NoteRemoveRequested(caller, owner, name)

    requires: owner.status = active
    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.role = owner
    requires: exists Note{owner: owner, name: name}

    ensures: not exists Note{owner: owner, name: name}
}

rule WriteJournal {
    when: JournalWriteRequested(caller, owner, text)

    requires: owner.status = active
    requires: caller.is_operator or caller.role = owner
    requires: text != ""
    requires: text.length <= config.max_journal_entry_length

    ensures: JournalEntry.created(owner: owner, text: text, at: now)

    @guidance
        -- Append only. Entries are never changed or removed. Reading
        -- gives the latest few, oldest first.
}

rule PutNewDoc {
    when: DocPutRequested(caller, path, content)

    requires: is_usable_doc_path(path)
    requires: not is_shown_path(path)   -- black box: path starts with shown/   -- black box: lower case names of letters, digits, dots, hyphens and underscores joined by /, at most 200 characters
    requires: content != ""
    requires: content.length <= config.max_doc_length
    requires: not exists Doc{path: path}
    -- A path that would be both a file and a folder is refused.
    requires: not doc_clash(path)   -- black box: an existing doc sits inside path/ or at a parent folder of path
    requires: writes_only_own_skills(caller, path)   -- black box: see the note on skills below

    ensures:
        let doc = Doc.created(path: path)
        DocVersion.created(
            doc: doc,
            at: now,
            actor: caller,
            content: content,
            removed: false
        )
}

rule PutDoc {
    when: DocPutRequested(caller, path, content)

    let doc = Doc{path: path}

    requires: exists doc
    requires: not is_shown_path(path)
    requires: content != ""
    requires: content.length <= config.max_doc_length
    requires: not doc_clash(path)
    requires: writes_only_own_skills(caller, path)
    -- Putting the content a doc already has records nothing. A removed
    -- doc has none, so putting it again brings it back.
    requires: not doc.is_present or doc.current.content != content

    ensures: DocVersion.created(
        doc: doc,
        at: now,
        actor: caller,
        content: content,
        removed: false
    )

    @guidance
        -- Every version is kept, written by whoever put it. The clash
        -- check ignores removed docs.
}

rule RemoveDoc {
    when: DocRemoveRequested(caller, doc)

    requires: doc.is_present
    requires: writes_only_own_skills(caller, doc.path)

    ensures: DocVersion.created(
        doc: doc,
        at: now,
        actor: caller,
        removed: true
    )

    @guidance
        -- Removal is a version too, so the history is kept. The doc
        -- disappears from the list, and as known before the removal it
        -- is still there.
}


-- The board
--
-- Every change to a card is an op, from a role's card_op, the operator's
-- relay card, or a client's _relay/cards/op, which is the operator's with
-- no labels. Each rule below writes a card/changed event carrying the op
-- as decided; its text elements take the caller's session labels and the
-- event's seq as their rev. An op that changes nothing (ticking an item
-- already done, writing the text already there) records nothing and says
-- so. An op naming a card, item, row or column that does not exist is
-- refused, saying so. So is an op with a parameter it does not know,
-- sessionId included, so a misspelled seen cannot pass unchecked. The
-- board's methods are the connection's, about no conversation.
--
-- seen: an op that changes text may carry the rev the client last saw.
-- It is refused when the text it changes was written after that rev, so
-- a stale edit never overwrites a newer one. A seen past the card's
-- rev is refused: no client can have read it. Ticks and cell states are
-- last writer wins.

rule AddCard {
    when: CardAddRequested(caller, kind, title, items, rows, columns, text)

    requires: caller.is_operator or (caller.is_role and not caller.is_public)
    requires: Cards.count(c => c.status = active) < config.max_active_cards
    requires: is_card_line(title)   -- black box: one line, 1 to card_line_length characters once trimmed
    -- A kind takes only its own contents.
    requires: kind = checklist implies (rows = null and columns = null and text = null
                                        and items.count <= config.max_checklist_items)
    requires: kind = tracker implies (items = null and text = null
                                      and rows.count <= config.max_tracker_rows
                                      and columns.count <= config.max_tracker_columns)
    requires: kind = note implies (items = null and rows = null and columns = null
                                   and text.length <= config.card_note_length)

    ensures: Card.created(
        kind: kind,
        title: title,
        owner: caller,
        added_at: now,
        status: active
    )

    @guidance
        -- The card's items, rows and columns are numbered from 1 in the
        -- order given, and the numbers are written into the card/added
        -- event with the next free one of each, so folding the log never
        -- invents an id. Nothing a role chooses becomes an id.
}

rule ChangeCard {
    when: CardOpRequested(caller, card, op)

    requires: caller.is_operator or (caller.is_role and not caller.is_public)
    requires: op.applies_to(card.kind)   -- black box: relay.cards/ops
    -- An archived card takes only restore.
    requires: card.status = active or op.name = restore
    requires: op.names_existing_elements(card)
    requires: op.seen = null or op.seen <= card.rev
    requires: not op.is_stale(card)   -- black box: op.seen < rev of the text it changes
    requires: op.within_limits(card)  -- black box: the card limits in config
    requires: op.name = restore implies Cards.count(c => c.status = active) < config.max_active_cards
    requires: op.changes(card)

    ensures: card.rev = now_seq

    @guidance
        -- retitle, archive, restore: any card. add, tick, untick, edit,
        -- remove: a checklist's items. set: a tracker cell, to open, done
        -- or skip; add_row, add_column, rename_row, rename_column,
        -- remove_row, remove_column. write: a note's text. Removing a
        -- row or column drops its cells. A new item, row or column takes
        -- the next number, written into the op.
}

rule ReadCard {
    when: CardRead(caller, card)

    requires: caller.is_operator or (caller.is_role and not caller.is_public)

    ensures: caller.session_labels = caller.session_labels + card.labels

    @guidance
        -- A house role is shown every card as it is. Removing a
        -- contaminated item, or the operator writing it again, takes
        -- contaminated off the card. A wake's or conversation's prompt
        -- lists the active cards, one line each with its progress, and
        -- the wake carries their titles' labels.
        -- A client is sent each card's wire form: every text field made
        -- visible, with its links broken and outsider set when
        -- contaminated. No text is stamped.
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

invariant TheLogIsGapless {
    -- seq starts at 1 and each event follows the one before.
    for event in Events:
        event.seq = 1 or exists Event{seq: event.seq - 1}
}

invariant TimeNeverDecreases {
    for a in Events:
        for b in Events:
            b.seq = a.seq + 1 implies b.at >= a.at
}

invariant EntryPointsDecideProvenance {
    -- Where text came in decides its labels. What the operator writes
    -- or pastes is hers and carries none: the command line, a line in a
    -- conversation, a pasted page or an attached resource in an ACP
    -- client. An ingestor's or a scout's text, and a tool's result,
    -- carry the labels relay.edn gives them.
    for event in Events where actor.is_operator:
        not has_contaminated(event.session_labels)
}

invariant PastesAreSanitized {
    -- Text the operator types, pastes or attaches is cleaned where it
    -- enters (relay.text/sanitize-input): the command line's writes, a
    -- conversation's prompt blocks and embedded resources, a card edit
    -- from a client, the operator's verified mail (a reply and a
    -- forward); the channels' replies call the same function. Mail from
    -- outside is left as it came. Invisible, bidi-control, tag, control
    -- and private-use characters are removed, line separators become line
    -- breaks, the rest is NFC, and printable ASCII is never touched.
    -- Cleaning twice gives the same text. Each change is told in one plain
    -- line: to the operator where they typed it, at the end of the memo
    -- for mail; mixed-alphabet words are flagged and kept.
    for text in OperatorText:
        sanitize(sanitize(text)) = sanitize(text)
        not has_hidden_characters(sanitize(text))
}

invariant NoWayOutOfTheHouse {
    -- No role that is not public is granted an egress tool, so nothing
    -- a house role reads can leave by one. A memo from a house role to a
    -- public role is public as written (SendAHouseMemoToAPublicRole), and
    -- what the public role does with it is held by ScoutsFetchOnlyWhatTheyWereShown.
    for role in Roles where not is_public:
        role.offered_tools.all(t => t.class != egress)
    for memo in Memos where recipient != null and recipient.is_public and sender.kind = role:
        memo.public
    -- A remote server's tool reaches a house role only as read or edit,
    -- so what it is given goes into the operator's own account there.
    for role in Roles where not is_public:
        role.offered_tools.all(t => not t.is_remote_mcp or t.class in {read, edit})
}

invariant ScoutsFetchOnlyWhatTheyWereShown {
    -- I4. relay runs every egress call itself. The settings refuse an
    -- egress tool of an MCP server, which agentloop would call itself,
    -- and any egress tool that is not an envelope tool of one of two
    -- shapes: a fetch tool, whose parameters are a url and otherwise
    -- numbers and yes-or-no values, or a search tool, which takes no url
    -- and whose free text is what the operator names in its queries and
    -- goes only to its search provider. No egress tool sends free text to
    -- an address, so a scout cannot publish what a house role wrote to
    -- it. relay runs a call only when its url
    -- argument, and in every other string the text from its first
    -- scheme:// to its end, appears verbatim in an earlier result of an
    -- egress tool in the same session, the sessions a resumed wake
    -- carries on included. That text in a query holds no space and no
    -- character a tool would escape, so a tool's echo of the query adds
    -- no address the session was not shown. Results of relay's own tools
    -- and of other tools do not count. Any other call is refused before
    -- it runs, with fixed text that quotes nothing of it. A redirect is
    -- reported, never followed, so its target is a new call under the
    -- same rule.
    for call in EgressCalls where call.ran:
        call.addresses.all(a => exists r in egress_results_before(call.session, call) where contains(r.text, a))
}

invariant StewardShell {
    -- sh runs a command in one container per data directory, named
    -- after it. relay composes every runner argument: no network, a
    -- read-only root, scratch and /tmp in memory, and each configured
    -- path mounted read-only at its own path. The settings name only the
    -- runner program, and refuse a mount that is, holds or sits in the
    -- data directory, the home directory or a known place for secrets,
    -- A path under /System/Volumes/Data is checked as the path it
    -- stands for, and when the container starts the check runs again
    -- with links resolved and by file identity.
    -- A command's time limit is kept by timeout inside the VM.
    for role in Roles where role.has_shell:
        not role.is_public
    -- What a command prints is private, and carries the labels of every
    -- session that ran a command since the container started and before
    -- this command ended, since any of them could have left text in
    -- scratch that it read.
    for result in ShellResults:
        "private" in result.labels
        includes_all(result.labels, result.container.scratch_labels)
}

invariant NothingTheStewardDoesDestroys {
    -- I7. The shell's mounts are read-only and the log is append-only.
    -- files_move never overwrites, deletes or copies, never moves a
    -- link or a writable folder, and never reaches outside the
    -- writable folders. Undoing every call in reverse order restores
    -- the tree byte for byte.
    for role in Roles where role.files != []:
        not role.is_public
    for call in MoveCalls:
        call.moves.all(m => inside(m.from, call.actor.files) and inside(m.to, call.actor.files))
}

invariant OldLogsStillFold {
    -- A log written by an older relay folds into the same state, its
    -- holds, permission requests, quarantine releases and trusts read
    -- as nothing. Kinds relay no longer writes are ignored, never
    -- refused. Two still keep old items as they were: anything a role
    -- or the dispatcher wrote before the log's first labels marker
    -- carries contaminated and private and is not public, since relay
    -- did not record what its writer had seen; and a declassified memo
    -- keeps the text the operator vetted, though not its publicity.
    for event in Events:
        folds(event)   -- black box: core/removed-event-kinds are skipped
}

invariant ARoleCallCarriesItsSessionsLabels {
    -- A role's tool call writes with the labels its session holds,
    -- which the harness sends with every call.
    for event in Events where actor.kind = role:
        includes_all(event.labels, event.session_labels)   -- black box: a superset of b
}

invariant NoEventDropsWhatItCopies {
    -- An event that copies or quotes text (a dead letter quoting a memo
    -- and a transcript, a routine's run, a message) carries that
    -- text's labels, whoever writes it, the dispatcher included.
    for event in Events:
        includes_all(event.labels, event.copied_labels)
}

invariant AWakeStartsWithTheLabelsOfItsPrompts {
    -- The role's id, title and instructions, the notes shown, the memos
    -- carried and the ids of their senders, the routines they are runs
    -- of, the journal entries, fact topics, skills and cards shown, and
    -- private for any relay content among them.
    for wake in Wakes:
        includes_all(wake.seed_labels, prompt_labels(wake))   -- black box: see guidance on RunWake
}

invariant NoSessionOfAPublicRoleHoldsPrivate {
    -- Its wakes and conversations start without private, and nothing it
    -- reads carries private.
    for wake in Wakes where wake.role.is_public:
        not has_private(wake.seed_labels)   -- black box: whether a set of labels holds private
            and wake.memos.all(m => not m.is_hidden)
}

invariant APublicItemNeverCarriesPrivate {
    for event in Events where public:
        not has_private(event.labels)
}

invariant AnEndedSessionIsNeverCarriedOn {
    for wake in Wakes where resumes != null:
        not session_was_ended_before(wake.resumes.session, wake.started_at)   -- black box: by a changed tool definition, or the role being made public
}

invariant OneWakeAtATime {
    for role in Roles:
        role.working_wakes.count <= 1
}

invariant OneConversationPerRole {
    for role in Roles:
        role.open_conversations.count <= 1
}

invariant OneTurnAtATime {
    -- A conversation holds its role while a turn runs, so no wake works
    -- alongside a running turn.
    for role in Roles:
        role.working_wakes.count = 0 or (role.open_conversations where turn = running).count = 0
}

invariant TurnsCountUp {
    for wake in Wakes where chat:
        wake.seen <= wake.turns
            and wake.turns_ended = (if wake.turn = running: wake.turns - 1 else: wake.turns)
            and (wake.turn = idle or wake.status = running)
}

invariant AWakeOnlyCarriesItsOwnRolesMemos {
    for wake in Wakes:
        wake.memos.all(m => m.recipient = wake.role)
}

invariant AConversationCarriesNoMemos {
    for wake in Wakes where chat:
        wake.memos.count = 0
}

invariant ARoutineHasAtMostOneOpenRun {
    for routine in Routines:
        (Memos where routine = routine and status = unread).count <= 1
}

invariant AttemptsStayWithinTheLimit {
    for memo in Memos:
        memo.attempts <= config.max_attempts
}

invariant AnOpenDeadLetterHasADeadMemo {
    for letter in DeadLetters where status = open:
        letter.memo.status = dead
}

invariant ASupersededMemoStaysDead {
    for memo in Memos where superseded_by != null:
        memo.status = dead
}

invariant ADeadLetterNotifiesTheOperatorAtMostOnce {
    -- Each dead letter is passed on exactly once: as a memo to the
    -- handler, or as one message to the operator, never both.
    for letter in DeadLetters:
        (Messages where dead_letter = letter).count <= 1
}

invariant EveryMemoToTheOperatorNotifiesOnce {
    for memo in Memos where recipient = null:
        (Messages where memo = memo).count = 1
}

invariant OnlyMemosToTheOperatorNotifyAsMemos {
    for message in Messages where origin = memo_for_operator:
        message.memo.recipient = null
}

invariant OnlyActiveRolesRun {
    for wake in Wakes where status = running:
        wake.role.status = active
}

invariant RoleIdsAreUnique {
    for a in Roles:
        for b in Roles:
            a != b implies a.id != b.id
}

invariant EveryFactHasItsFirstVersion {
    -- Versions are only ever added, never changed or dropped. See the
    -- Facts contract.
    for fact in Facts:
        fact.versions.count >= 1
}

invariant ValidityIsInOrder {
    for version in FactVersions:
        version.valid_from = null or version.valid_to = null or version.valid_to > version.valid_from
}

invariant SupersessionLinksRunBothWays {
    -- Until the successor is retracted, which puts the old fact back.
    for fact in Facts where supersedes != null:
        fact.is_retracted or fact.supersedes.versions.any(v => v.superseded_by = fact)
}

invariant EveryDocHasAVersion {
    for doc in Docs:
        doc.versions.count >= 1
}

invariant NoDocIsBothFileAndFolder {
    for a in Docs where is_present:
        for b in Docs where is_present:
            a != b implies not is_inside(a.path, b.path)   -- black box: a is under b as a folder
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

actor Operator {
    identified_by: Caller where kind = operator
}

actor Dispatcher {
    identified_by: Caller where kind = dispatcher
}

actor RoleActor {
    identified_by: Caller where kind = role
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface Inbound {
    facing caller: Caller

    provides:
        RoleAddRequested(caller, id, title?, instructions, reports_to?, harness?, model?)
            when caller.is_operator or caller.may_add
        RoleUpdateRequested(caller, role, title?, instructions?, reports_to?, harness?, model?)
            when caller.is_operator or caller.may_add
        RoleRemoveRequested(caller, role)
            when caller.is_operator or caller.may_add
        MemoSendRequested(caller, recipient, subject, body)
        MemoToOperatorSendRequested(caller, subject, body)
        MemoCloseRequested(caller, memo, outcome)
        MemoBlockRequested(caller, memo, explanation)
            when caller.kind = role
        RetryRequested(caller, role)
            when caller.can_requeue
        RoutineWriteRequested(caller, owner, name, schedule, instructions)
            when caller.is_operator or caller.kind = role
        RoutineRemoveRequested(caller, routine)
            when caller.is_operator or caller.kind = role
        WakeRequested(caller, role, note?, pid, pid_start)
            when caller.is_operator or caller.is_dispatcher
        ConversationRequested(caller, role, note?, pid, pid_start)
            when caller.is_operator
        TurnRequested(caller, wake, session)
            when caller.is_operator
        ConversationSeen(caller, wake, turn)
            when caller.is_operator
        FactAddRequested(caller, topic?, text, valid_from?, valid_to?)
        FactSupersedeRequested(caller, fact, topic?, text, valid_from?, valid_to?)
        FactCorrectRequested(caller, fact, why, topic?, text?, valid_from?, valid_to?)
        FactRetractRequested(caller, fact, why)
        NoteWriteRequested(caller, owner, name, text)
        NoteRemoveRequested(caller, owner, name)
        JournalWriteRequested(caller, owner, text)
        DocPutRequested(caller, path, content)
        DocRemoveRequested(caller, doc)
        DisplayShown(caller, ref, title, body, sources, call)
            when caller.kind = role
        ToolCallRequested(caller, tool, arguments)
            when caller.kind = role
        FactRevertRequested(caller, fact, version)
            when caller.is_operator
        DocRevertRequested(caller, doc, version)
            when caller.is_operator
        WakeFlagRequested(caller, wake, value, note?)
            when caller.is_operator

    @guarantee EveryWriteGoesThroughOneInboundPath
        -- Whoever asks, whether the operator at the command line, a role
        -- through a tool, or the dispatcher, a change is a command
        -- submitted here. It is decided against the current state and
        -- appended in one step under the log's lock, so two writers can
        -- never both act on a state that one of them has already
        -- changed. A command that is refused writes nothing. Anything
        -- that depends on the clock or the settings is worked out when
        -- the command is decided and written into the events, so
        -- replaying the log never consults either.

    @guarantee TimeNeverGoesBackwards
        -- An event is recorded no earlier than the one before it. If
        -- the clock reads earlier than the last event, the last
        -- event's time is used.

    @guarantee EntityIdsAreTheSeqOfTheirCreatingEvent
        -- Memo 42 is the memo that event 42 sent. Role ids are
        -- chosen; every other id is a seq.

    @guarantee CallerIsNeverGuessed
        -- A command run by a harness acts as the role that harness was
        -- started for: the harness sets the role on every tool call,
        -- and a command run with it set acts as that role and nothing
        -- more, so it can never act as the operator. A command run by
        -- anyone else acts as the operator. The caller must be the
        -- operator, the dispatcher or an active role.

    @guarantee ReplayNeedsOnlyTheLog
        -- The state can always be rebuilt from the log. A log with an
        -- event type this version does not know is refused rather
        -- than read wrongly.
}

surface Clock {
    provides:
        DispatcherTicks(lost_wakes)

    @guidance
        -- Something outside relay ticks the dispatcher about once a
        -- minute. A tick ends wakes whose process is gone, fires due
        -- routines, trips the runaway guard, reports outages that
        -- outlasted the patience, delivers messages that are due,
        -- polls the ingest sources and sends one message for the new
        -- GitHub items from people, then starts a wake for each role
        -- with work waiting. Last, it makes the daily note when one is due.
        -- The first four are one event append in this order; rules are
        -- not ordered here, but a later step sees an earlier step's
        -- events.
}

surface HarnessBoundary {
    provides:
        WakeReported(wake, outcome, exit?, crashed, cut_short, session?, said?, transcript?, resets_at?, labels?)
        DispatchedWakeSpawned(role, pid, pid_start)

    contracts:
        demands HarnessAdapter
}

surface ConversationBoundary {
    provides:
        TurnReported(wake, stop_reason)

    @guidance
        -- Each session/prompt from a client asks for a turn
        -- (TurnRequested, as the operator) before it reaches the agent.
        -- One refused because the role is busy waits, and is asked for
        -- again whenever the log changes; one refused for another reason
        -- is answered with relay's reason as a JSON-RPC error and goes no
        -- further. The agent's answer to a prompt that started a turn
        -- reports the turn's end with its stopReason, or error for an
        -- error, before any client sees the answer.
        -- relay never asks a client for permission: an agent's
        -- session/request_permission (agentloop sends none) is answered
        -- cancelled and no client sees it.
        -- A display block's own text reaches the client inert (hidden
        -- characters escaped, links defanged, fenced), made from the
        -- display under _meta, which a capable client shows apart.
        -- relay, agentloop and relay-tui read every line by one strict
        -- JSON rule: one object in valid UTF-8, no byte order mark,
        -- only whitespace after it, no member name twice at any depth,
        -- no unpaired surrogate, nesting at most 128, number literals at
        -- most 1000 characters, exponents within -9999..9999 by value,
        -- names matched exactly, numbers exact.
        -- A line that breaks it is passed on in neither direction. An
        -- agent message whose method starts with
        -- _relay/ never reaches the client, and neither does a response
        -- from the agent unless it answers a request of the client's that
        -- relay passed on and that the agent has not answered yet. Every
        -- other line passes unchanged.
}

surface ConversationService {
    -- relay.hub, carried out by relay serve or, with no service running,
    -- by relay acp in its own process.

    @guidance
        -- Clients are connections: relay acp's stdio, the service's
        -- Unix socket, which only the operator's user can open, or, when
        -- relay.edn configures it, the service's WebSocket listener on
        -- 127.0.0.1, which the operator publishes on the tailnet. A
        -- WebSocket client is let in only with the token the service
        -- read at startup (compared in constant time) and with no Origin
        -- header unless the operator allowed that origin; a refusal is a
        -- bare status that says nothing about relay. Each WebSocket is a
        -- connection with no role; its session/new without a role goes to the configured
        -- default role. One text message is one line; a binary message
        -- or one over 8 MB closes it. Every transport shares one cap on
        -- connections and one bound on what waits for a client. A
        -- connection through relay acp says first, in a _relay/connect
        -- line relay acp writes itself, which role it is for; relay takes that line only
        -- as a socket connection's first, never later and never on stdio.
        -- A role has at most one live conversation (OpenConversation).
        -- session/new for a role opens it, or attaches the connection to
        -- the live one; session/load attaches by session; nothing ended
        -- is reopened. An attaching connection gets the conversation's
        -- updates so far, at most a bounded amount, with consecutive text
        -- chunks of one kind merged and the session's latest labels (and
        -- usage) before any of them whatever was dropped, so no text is
        -- shown with fewer labels than it carries, then _relay/replayed,
        -- which says whether older updates were dropped, then every later
        -- update, with no gap and no duplicate. Each prompt also reaches
        -- the other attached connections as the operator's message.
        -- Every request a connection sends is answered once; relay gives
        -- each request it passes on an id of its own, so connections'
        -- ids never meet. A turn keeps running when every connection has
        -- gone. The service keeps a conversation until the operator ends
        -- it (_relay/conversations/end) or the service stops; relay acp in
        -- its own process ends its conversations when its connection
        -- ends. Stopping the service ends every conversation, a turn in
        -- progress with it (EndTurn, ended), and records it; one a dead
        -- service left is ended as lost (EndLostWakes) by the next.
        -- Every request relay has taken and not yet answered is one
        -- record, from the moment it is taken to its answer; its id stays
        -- the connection's while the record lives, and one left by a
        -- connection that went away stays until its answer comes. A
        -- conversation takes a bounded number of them, orphans included,
        -- and a connection a bounded number too. session/cancel cancels
        -- for the session, whichever attached connection sends it: every
        -- waiting prompt and the running turn. The board is relay's and
        -- the connection's, open to a client with no conversation: its
        -- methods take no sessionId and refuse one, and relay sends each
        -- subscribed connection the cards that changed since what it was
        -- last sent. An end of a turn relay could not record
        -- is tried again until it is; until then no other turn of the role
        -- starts, and the operator is told once.
        -- _relay/roles gives every role's status (relay.roster, plus a
        -- turn that waits shown as queued) and then the whole list again
        -- whenever any of it changes.
}

surface MessageBoundary {
    provides:
        DeliverySucceeded(messages, channel)
        DeliveryFailed(messages, channel, error)
        -- _relay/messages: every message, newest first, then
        -- _relay/messages/changed for each one made or changed since.
        ClientMessages(messages)

    contracts:
        demands Channel

    @guarantee NothingElseReachesThem
        -- The operator is told things only through messages, and every
        -- message is in the client whatever its other deliveries did.
        -- They never have to look anywhere to find out whether the
        -- roles need them. Nothing they receive names a role, a tool,
        -- a label or a class unless they asked.
}

surface TheRecord {
    exposes:
        Events

    @guidance
        -- Every change is an event. Anyone may read the log; only the
        -- inbound path appends to it.
}

surface RoleTools {
    facing caller: Caller

    contracts:
        demands Tools
        demands Facts
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Open Questions
------------------------------------------------------------

open question "Closing a memo proves the role dealt with it, not that they dealt with it well. Who reviews outcomes, and how often?"
